WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Downloaded from CINEFREAK.NET

00:02:25.441 --> 00:02:30.754
<i>♪ Beyond the distant miles ♪</i>

00:02:30.886 --> 00:02:35.279
<i>♪ Are you waiting there? ♪</i>

00:02:35.304 --> 00:02:42.698
<i>♪ O star, for the night to finally arrive? ♪</i>

00:02:42.727 --> 00:02:48.753
<i>♪ To look down upon this earth below? ♪</i>

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:09.320
<i>♪ Beyond the distant miles
Are you waiting there ♪</i>

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:14.570
<i>♪ O star, for the night to finally arrive? ♪</i>

00:03:14.956 --> 00:03:20.156
<i>♪ To look down upon this earth below? ♪</i>

00:03:20.536 --> 00:03:23.070
<i>♪ When the veil of sunlight fades ♪</i>

00:03:23.333 --> 00:03:26.386
<i>♪ And the streetlights begin to glow ♪</i>

00:03:26.411 --> 00:03:31.556
<i>♪ O star, do you yearn ♪</i>

00:03:31.955 --> 00:03:37.175
<i>♪ To see these streets below? ♪</i>

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:43.230
<i>♪ When the silent sky falls asleep ♪</i>

00:03:43.255 --> 00:03:48.438
<i>♪ Why do you stand there all alone? ♪</i>

00:03:54.437 --> 00:04:00.190
<i>♪ Don't remain there
Like a tiny speck upon the sky-wall ♪</i>

00:04:00.241 --> 00:04:05.437
<i>♪ Come down and see the night ♪</i>

00:04:05.787 --> 00:04:11.340
<i>♪ Let us wander through these
Beautiful streets ♪</i>

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:17.180
<i>♪ A thousand sleepless eyes ♪</i>

00:04:17.205 --> 00:04:22.310
<i>♪ Will sparkle like pearls ♪</i>

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:30.683
<i>♪ Within them,
We shall sow the seeds of desires ♪</i>

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:49.864
<i>♪ There is another world
Hidden deep within them ♪</i>

00:04:50.162 --> 00:04:55.522
<i>♪ Filled with longing and tender sorrow ♪</i>

00:04:55.863 --> 00:05:01.483
<i>♪ Even as you burn,
You still shimmer and shine ♪</i>

00:05:01.508 --> 00:05:07.158
<i>♪ I turn your weeping face
Into a tender flower ♪</i>

00:05:07.183 --> 00:05:12.441
<i>♪ And here I wander,
Riding the chariot of dreams ♪</i>

00:05:13.276 --> 00:05:15.484
Hey man! Are you blind?

00:05:15.589 --> 00:05:18.589
You'd be dead right now
if I hadn't hit the brakes on time.

00:05:19.232 --> 00:05:21.325
Huh? You're just gonna walk away?

00:05:22.406 --> 00:05:23.614
Hey!!

00:05:23.781 --> 00:05:25.823
Is he dumb?

00:05:26.031 --> 00:05:27.406
Hey!

00:05:27.672 --> 00:05:29.089
Or just high?

00:05:30.031 --> 00:05:31.965
Dude, are you high? Huh?

00:05:31.989 --> 00:05:34.781
I was high too, but that sudden brake
sobered me up real quick.

00:05:35.156 --> 00:05:36.448
Let's grab a drink together.

00:05:36.473 --> 00:05:38.387
I've got booze in the car. Shall I get it?

00:05:42.364 --> 00:05:44.448
I was actually looking for some company.

00:05:45.489 --> 00:05:48.772
Got whiskey, got a glass...

00:05:49.705 --> 00:05:52.282
I'm going to get my silent friend
completely drunk tonight.

00:06:04.937 --> 00:06:07.917
Hey! Are you ditching me? Huh?

00:06:09.531 --> 00:06:12.340
It's the first of the month,
I'm offering you free booze,

00:06:12.365 --> 00:06:14.038
and you're throwing attitude?

00:06:16.614 --> 00:06:18.689
Show me attitude,

00:06:18.714 --> 00:06:20.131
and I'll run you over right here.

00:06:20.156 --> 00:06:22.400
It's pitch dark, not a soul will ever know.

00:06:29.156 --> 00:06:30.452
Scared now, aren't you?

00:06:30.531 --> 00:06:31.745
Come here, brother!

00:06:31.829 --> 00:06:34.911
Come on over, nice and slow!

00:06:35.448 --> 00:06:36.793
Come, come, come.

00:06:36.837 --> 00:06:40.216
I'm getting you totally drunk tonight!

00:06:41.031 --> 00:06:42.391
Bless me, my forefathers!

00:06:47.531 --> 00:06:48.783
What the hell is this, man?

00:06:57.198 --> 00:06:58.600
What?

00:07:43.992 --> 00:07:45.499
'CRIME STORIES'

00:07:45.951 --> 00:07:49.034
Boban, a businessman, was
brutally murdered on the street.

00:07:49.059 --> 00:07:52.880
You just watched our investigative report
on the incident.

00:07:53.015 --> 00:07:55.960
Now, let me draw your attention
to a similar case.

00:07:56.031 --> 00:07:59.913
Justin, a young man, was murdered
at this exact same spot,

00:07:59.938 --> 00:08:01.514
a few weeks ago.

00:08:01.976 --> 00:08:05.704
Justin, who was riding a bike,
was found dead

00:08:05.728 --> 00:08:09.103
his head violently smashed
against a concrete post.

00:08:09.268 --> 00:08:13.193
The striking similarity between
the two murders,

00:08:13.559 --> 00:08:15.179
and the police suspecting that

00:08:15.204 --> 00:08:17.139
both were committed
by the same person,

00:08:17.184 --> 00:08:19.170
makes this case highly mysterious.

00:08:19.643 --> 00:08:22.923
Are these incidents pointing towards
a serial killer?

00:08:22.976 --> 00:08:24.696
Maria is on a roll today.

00:08:25.659 --> 00:08:28.327
Boban's case is also being handled by
the special investigation team...

00:08:28.351 --> 00:08:29.471
Hey, turn it off.

00:08:29.496 --> 00:08:32.923
Ied by Circle Inspector Christy,
who is also handling Justin's case.

00:08:34.167 --> 00:08:35.201
Listen,

00:08:35.226 --> 00:08:37.076
you better catch the culprit soon.

00:08:38.184 --> 00:08:39.802
How's the investigation going?

00:08:41.196 --> 00:08:42.743
I just updated your brother.

00:08:42.768 --> 00:08:44.450
Now I have to report to you as well?

00:08:45.385 --> 00:08:48.491
Hey, make me your
special ginger tea, please.

00:08:49.059 --> 00:08:50.443
Food is ready. Let's eat.

00:08:50.476 --> 00:08:52.849
Not now. Gotta make a few calls first.

00:09:05.809 --> 00:09:06.909
Hello, Christy.

00:09:06.934 --> 00:09:09.624
I caught a bit of your program.
It was good.

00:09:10.434 --> 00:09:12.993
The full episode drops
on YouTube tomorrow.

00:09:13.101 --> 00:09:14.246
I'll send you the link.

00:09:14.351 --> 00:09:15.479
Okay, I'll check it out.

00:09:15.618 --> 00:09:19.057
Listen, I'm worried I'll get in trouble
for sharing investigation details with you.

00:09:19.101 --> 00:09:22.612
Why? I haven't revealed
anything sensitive on the show.

00:09:23.268 --> 00:09:27.262
We can't officially confirm
it's a serial killer yet.

00:09:27.434 --> 00:09:29.574
Think about your viewers.

00:09:29.643 --> 00:09:31.614
Do you realise
how much this could panic them?

00:09:32.351 --> 00:09:33.569
Of course.

00:09:33.726 --> 00:09:36.370
They watch "Crime Stories"
for the thrill of it.

00:09:36.816 --> 00:09:37.826
Besides,

00:09:37.851 --> 00:09:39.961
my viewers are just the new-gen version
of the readers

00:09:39.985 --> 00:09:41.887
who made my dad's crime novels a hit.

00:09:42.184 --> 00:09:43.776
To them, it's purely entertainment.

00:09:44.156 --> 00:09:46.143
Come on, is a TV show the same as a novel?

00:09:46.226 --> 00:09:48.969
Your dad, Stephen, only based
his books on cold cases.

00:09:49.309 --> 00:09:53.101
I don't think my show is going to affect
your investigation at all.

00:09:53.226 --> 00:09:55.840
Plus, I firmly believe
it's the work of a psycho killer.

00:09:55.934 --> 00:09:57.206
Hmm. Alright.

00:10:09.893 --> 00:10:11.285
- Good morning, sir.
- Good morning.

00:10:11.309 --> 00:10:12.549
- Is everybody here?
- Yes, sir.

00:10:12.678 --> 00:10:13.869
Sojan was on night duty, right?

00:10:13.893 --> 00:10:16.168
Yes, sir. But he waited back
for the meeting.

00:10:16.268 --> 00:10:17.869
Okay, let's get started.

00:10:22.643 --> 00:10:25.000
Sojan sir, wake up.

00:10:25.061 --> 00:10:27.661
Sir is here. You can go home and sleep
after the meeting. Come on.

00:10:36.579 --> 00:10:37.679
Yes.

00:10:38.851 --> 00:10:39.971
Shoot.

00:10:40.768 --> 00:10:44.868
We cross-checked all the numbers
from the cyber cell's report.

00:10:45.101 --> 00:10:48.289
We don't think the killer
used a mobile phone.

00:10:48.585 --> 00:10:51.713
We questioned several people
around both crime scenes.

00:10:51.817 --> 00:10:53.910
Checked their backgrounds too.

00:10:54.059 --> 00:10:56.591
But, we found no one suspicious.

00:10:56.893 --> 00:10:58.319
Sir, the team has a suggestion.

00:10:58.351 --> 00:11:01.576
After a lot of effort, we've identified
six people connected to Justin's murder.

00:11:01.601 --> 00:11:04.078
But we haven't been able to
bring them in for questioning yet.

00:11:04.766 --> 00:11:07.692
Look, these six are suspects
in the Justin murder case.

00:11:07.976 --> 00:11:11.249
We have evidence pointing to
the same killer in both cases.

00:11:11.351 --> 00:11:13.452
That's why I asked you
to hold off on questioning them.

00:11:13.476 --> 00:11:14.659
What we need to know now is,

00:11:14.684 --> 00:11:18.672
if any of these six suspects
have links to Boban.

00:11:18.697 --> 00:11:20.795
I asked you to look into it,
but you came up empty.

00:11:20.851 --> 00:11:23.571
It's not that, sir. If we interrogate them
properly,

00:11:23.595 --> 00:11:25.676
we might get a solid lead.

00:11:26.226 --> 00:11:28.066
Sir, should we bring them in?

00:11:28.184 --> 00:11:31.034
- Jenny, did you get Boban's call logs?
- Yes, sir.

00:11:31.059 --> 00:11:32.826
Who was the last person he spoke to?

00:11:32.851 --> 00:11:36.774
A woman named Anitha was the last person
he called that night.

00:11:36.934 --> 00:11:39.499
They used to speak regularly
late at night.

00:11:39.976 --> 00:11:43.742
Anitha's husband, Jayan,
used to be Boban's driver.

00:11:44.601 --> 00:11:45.776
What's his background?

00:11:45.809 --> 00:11:47.160
Well, sir...

00:11:47.184 --> 00:11:49.702
Our team is heading there today
to question Jayan and Anitha, sir.

00:11:49.726 --> 00:11:54.129
But there's no evidence
linking them to Justin so far.

00:11:55.105 --> 00:11:58.632
We need a suspect list for Boban,
just like we have for Justin.

00:11:58.726 --> 00:12:01.726
We have to cross-check
for any common links,

00:12:02.616 --> 00:12:05.201
rule out the rest, and
narrow down the list.

00:12:05.226 --> 00:12:06.394
Then we catch the killer.

00:12:06.419 --> 00:12:08.670
Rounding suspects up blindly won't help.

00:12:09.601 --> 00:12:12.684
- Sojan, we need to step up night patrols.
- Sir.

00:12:12.726 --> 00:12:14.876
Deploy more men across the city.

00:12:16.108 --> 00:12:18.618
- Identify buildings with CCTV cameras.
- Sir.

00:12:18.706 --> 00:12:21.538
Explain the gravity of the situation,
and secure the footage.

00:12:21.601 --> 00:12:24.613
I'll coordinate with Manoj sir
for the official clearances. Okay?

00:12:24.726 --> 00:12:26.061
Alright, get to it.

00:12:45.931 --> 00:12:47.845
Hello. Where is driver Jayan's house?

00:12:48.051 --> 00:12:50.038
Jayan's? Go straight
and take the second left.

00:12:50.206 --> 00:12:51.483
Second left, got it.

00:12:53.768 --> 00:12:55.811
Justin had a lot of enemies in town.

00:12:55.893 --> 00:12:58.046
But Boban was the exact opposite.

00:12:58.351 --> 00:13:00.532
People generally spoke highly of him.

00:13:00.556 --> 00:13:03.371
His only flaw was his heavy drinking.

00:13:06.059 --> 00:13:09.063
What if the same killer was hired
to murder both of them?

00:13:09.088 --> 00:13:10.949
Even then, the fingerprints would match.

00:13:11.018 --> 00:13:13.817
Are you suggesting a contract killer?

00:13:14.643 --> 00:13:17.123
If the people who hired the killer
aren't connected,

00:13:17.268 --> 00:13:18.948
we won't be able to link the cases, right?

00:13:20.101 --> 00:13:22.143
It's unlikely to be a seasoned criminal.

00:13:22.351 --> 00:13:25.934
We didn't find any fingerprint matches
in our database.

00:13:27.926 --> 00:13:31.801
If one more head gets smashed,
the whole game changes.

00:13:32.059 --> 00:13:34.298
We'll lose control over the case.
You know that, right?

00:13:35.726 --> 00:13:38.351
Sir, we really need to step up
the night patrols.

00:13:38.488 --> 00:13:40.907
We're going to need more manpower
and vehicles.

00:13:41.393 --> 00:13:43.559
We are doing our best
to prevent another murder.

00:13:44.518 --> 00:13:46.059
Don't worry about the logistics.

00:13:46.101 --> 00:13:47.532
I will make the arrangements.

00:13:48.873 --> 00:13:49.826
Listen,

00:13:49.851 --> 00:13:51.734
if the pressure from the top gets too much,

00:13:51.759 --> 00:13:54.520
identify a couple of suspects we
can bring in to manage the situation.

00:13:54.691 --> 00:13:55.945
And...

00:13:56.059 --> 00:13:59.143
Look at this as a chance
to clear your bad reputation.

00:13:59.684 --> 00:14:03.136
Solving high-profile cases like this
makes you a star.

00:14:04.093 --> 00:14:05.293
Sir.

00:14:07.309 --> 00:14:09.671
If you succeed,
I can take some of the credit

00:14:09.696 --> 00:14:11.458
as long as I am in the department.

00:14:11.726 --> 00:14:14.837
But if you fail,
I won't be able to protect you.

00:14:15.246 --> 00:14:16.991
Especially since you're my brother-in-law.

00:14:17.019 --> 00:14:18.049
You understand, right?

00:14:22.518 --> 00:14:24.323
I worked for him for almost four years.

00:14:24.601 --> 00:14:27.428
He's the one who paid
for my son's treatment.

00:14:27.851 --> 00:14:29.541
Did Boban visit you here?

00:14:29.643 --> 00:14:33.400
Yes, he didn't have children,
so he was very fond of my son.

00:14:37.684 --> 00:14:38.923
Come here.

00:14:39.269 --> 00:14:41.883
You say Boban was such a great guy,

00:14:42.179 --> 00:14:44.172
- yet you're working for Safar now?
- Yes.

00:14:44.434 --> 00:14:48.418
From what we gathered,
Safar was Boban's only enemy.

00:14:49.768 --> 00:14:51.210
That's not true, sir.

00:14:51.685 --> 00:14:54.146
Boban sir could sort out an issue
with anyone over a drink.

00:14:54.170 --> 00:14:55.371
Didn't matter who it was.

00:14:56.096 --> 00:14:59.359
When Safar needed
a reliable driver for long trips,

00:14:59.516 --> 00:15:01.218
Boban sir himself recommended me.

00:15:01.601 --> 00:15:03.371
There was no bad blood between them.

00:15:03.476 --> 00:15:06.788
He used to call my phone
just to talk to my son, madam.

00:15:06.976 --> 00:15:08.634
He loved him dearly.

00:15:08.976 --> 00:15:11.826
My son has been devastated since
he heard about Boban uncle's death.

00:15:11.851 --> 00:15:14.528
He still cries about it.

00:15:16.184 --> 00:15:18.055
What about you? Aren't you sad?

00:15:26.952 --> 00:15:29.159
You'll see a signboard for "Marakkudi"
on your right.

00:15:29.184 --> 00:15:31.942
It's barely a kilometre from there.

00:15:32.268 --> 00:15:34.445
I've shared my live location.
Just follow that.

00:15:34.726 --> 00:15:35.772
Okay.

00:15:50.664 --> 00:15:51.971
Is this the place you mentioned?

00:15:52.018 --> 00:15:53.164
Yes.

00:15:54.434 --> 00:15:56.951
This house was in the news 10 years ago

00:15:56.975 --> 00:15:59.310
as the crime scene of the 'Marakkudi'
mass murder case.

00:16:06.348 --> 00:16:10.321
['Bekarar Karke Hume' song
from 'Bees Saal Baad' playing]

00:16:52.703 --> 00:16:55.635
He trespassed into the house
and killed four people,

00:16:55.931 --> 00:16:59.264
including six-year-old Fathima
who was playing in her room.

00:17:06.183 --> 00:17:09.444
The police caught the culprit
on the sixth day itself.

00:17:09.809 --> 00:17:11.181
A man named Nawas.

00:17:11.476 --> 00:17:12.860
He is still in prison.

00:17:13.476 --> 00:17:14.909
What was his motive?

00:17:16.559 --> 00:17:18.796
What do you think, Christy? Tell me.

00:17:19.203 --> 00:17:20.243
Theft?

00:17:20.268 --> 00:17:22.975
There was no theft or assault.
Any other guesses?

00:17:24.309 --> 00:17:27.643
Could be a financial dispute
or an extramarital affair?

00:17:29.351 --> 00:17:33.259
Even Nawas doesn't know
why he killed those four people.

00:17:33.726 --> 00:17:37.370
He didn't even have a petty case
against him before this incident.

00:17:40.976 --> 00:17:45.086
Which means, Christy, a crime
doesn't always need a logical motive.

00:17:47.059 --> 00:17:50.851
If it's a psycho killer, even they
might not know why they're killing.

00:18:33.226 --> 00:18:34.946
- Where is the superintendent?
- Over there.

00:18:36.059 --> 00:18:38.379
After his conviction,
he was under treatment for two years.

00:18:38.726 --> 00:18:40.118
He's been normal since then.

00:18:40.476 --> 00:18:42.435
He has a chance at parole now.

00:18:43.184 --> 00:18:44.993
He'll be able to see the outside world.

00:18:45.059 --> 00:18:46.916
Should we really drag up the past
at a time like this?

00:18:46.940 --> 00:18:48.901
It's for a new case, sir.

00:18:49.087 --> 00:18:51.134
If I could just speak to someone like him…

00:18:52.101 --> 00:18:53.789
By the way, what's that guy's name?

00:18:54.393 --> 00:18:57.154
The one who used to smash the heads
of people sleeping on the streets.

00:18:58.143 --> 00:18:59.974
- What was his name?
- Suresh, sir.

00:18:59.999 --> 00:19:01.682
Yes, let's call him.

00:19:02.059 --> 00:19:04.026
Go ask him to come here.

00:19:04.054 --> 00:19:06.334
I will try, sir.
But it all depends on his mood.

00:19:06.434 --> 00:19:10.102
No, sir. Let's not force anyone.

00:19:10.184 --> 00:19:11.904
I need someone who is willing to cooperate.

00:19:13.184 --> 00:19:14.527
Nawas is a good man.

00:19:15.059 --> 00:19:16.315
He will cooperate.

00:19:17.059 --> 00:19:19.643
But... should we...?

00:19:22.933 --> 00:19:24.640
It's okay, sir. I understand.

00:19:29.643 --> 00:19:32.409
Nawas, the culprit in the Marakkudi case,
was caught by

00:19:32.434 --> 00:19:34.514
a police officer named Swamy.

00:19:34.643 --> 00:19:35.927
Let's try to find him.

00:19:36.101 --> 00:19:38.119
He must have a lot of experience
with such criminals.

00:19:38.143 --> 00:19:40.730
My dad worked with him on an old case.

00:19:40.851 --> 00:19:43.131
My dad says Swamy is crazy.

00:19:43.684 --> 00:19:46.477
Who wouldn't go crazy
dealing with such criminals?

00:19:47.726 --> 00:19:50.176
Heard he got fed up and quit the force.
Anyway, let's see.

00:19:50.226 --> 00:19:54.046
Sir, if the killer is a psycho,
we need to dig deeper into this mindset.

00:19:54.101 --> 00:19:56.076
Having someone like him
would be a huge help.

00:19:56.101 --> 00:19:59.316
Will the killer just sit tight
while we study and figure things out?

00:19:59.684 --> 00:20:01.142
He will strike again.

00:20:01.393 --> 00:20:04.143
Sir, both incidents happened at night.
In deserted areas...

00:20:04.518 --> 00:20:07.699
Neither victim used that route regularly.

00:20:08.228 --> 00:20:13.157
It doesn't look like the killer
planned this and waited for them.

00:20:13.559 --> 00:20:18.280
It seems more like the victims
accidentally crossed paths with him.

00:20:18.684 --> 00:20:21.524
In that case, we need to increase
patrols in all isolated areas.

00:20:21.549 --> 00:20:22.508
Sir.

00:20:22.559 --> 00:20:24.893
Question anyone who looks suspicious.

00:20:25.934 --> 00:20:27.214
Don't spare anyone.

00:20:27.451 --> 00:20:29.659
I don't want him slipping through
our fingers again.

00:20:29.684 --> 00:20:30.738
Understood, sir.

00:20:34.518 --> 00:20:36.771
Looks like you've done your homework.

00:20:37.033 --> 00:20:39.880
Sir, Maria from "Crime Story"
gave me some files.

00:20:40.434 --> 00:20:45.062
Her father, Stephen, has studied
many psycho killers.

00:20:45.226 --> 00:20:48.463
Most of his novels are based on
his research.

00:20:48.893 --> 00:20:52.547
I'm not sure if reading novels
is the right way to investigate a case.

00:20:52.809 --> 00:20:53.993
These aren't novels, sir.

00:20:54.018 --> 00:20:55.935
They are psychological studies.

00:20:56.184 --> 00:20:57.538
Okay.

00:20:57.768 --> 00:20:59.395
Don't dismiss anything.

00:20:59.768 --> 00:21:01.249
- Look into it anyway.
- Yes, sir.

00:21:03.018 --> 00:21:05.218
- If I track down Swamy, I'll let you know.
- Okay, sir.

00:21:10.874 --> 00:21:12.493
The stories about Swamy are exaggerated.

00:21:12.518 --> 00:21:14.033
He solved a case by pure luck,

00:21:14.057 --> 00:21:15.955
and the media blew his image
out of proportion.

00:21:16.018 --> 00:21:18.636
But he caught Nawas in the "Marakkudi" case
in just six days.

00:21:18.726 --> 00:21:21.059
I heard a rumour that
he uses black magic to solve cases.

00:21:21.226 --> 00:21:24.141
He probably just tortured
all the suspects until someone confessed.

00:21:24.226 --> 00:21:25.785
Back in his day,
that was standard procedure.

00:21:25.809 --> 00:21:27.287
The Marakkudi case wasn't like that.

00:21:27.351 --> 00:21:29.011
A six-year-old girl was murdered.

00:21:29.226 --> 00:21:32.270
So Swamy investigated recent deaths
of kids around that same age.

00:21:32.684 --> 00:21:33.689
That led him to Nawas,

00:21:33.714 --> 00:21:36.244
who was severely depressed after
his own daughter's unexpected death.

00:21:36.268 --> 00:21:37.333
Nawas was a plumber.

00:21:37.393 --> 00:21:40.465
All four victims were hit on the head
with a pipe wrench.

00:21:41.031 --> 00:21:43.469
The facts lined up perfectly,
and the case was closed.

00:21:43.739 --> 00:21:45.873
That's exactly my point, sir.
It was just lucky guesswork.

00:21:45.897 --> 00:21:49.757
Making the right guess that quickly
is a skill in itself, isn't it?

00:21:50.059 --> 00:21:51.185
Yes, sir.

00:21:51.559 --> 00:21:53.292
We will step up the night patrols, sir.

00:21:53.726 --> 00:21:55.606
The killer might
just walk right into our hands.

00:21:55.639 --> 00:21:57.353
Yes. Good night.

00:21:57.478 --> 00:21:58.578
Sir.

00:22:12.228 --> 00:22:14.106
Have you confirmed it's a psycho killer?

00:22:14.131 --> 00:22:17.131
Not yet. We're keeping all options open.

00:22:18.715 --> 00:22:20.788
Anyway, my brother Manoj is very impressed.

00:22:20.971 --> 00:22:23.076
I know you'll crack it this time. I'm sure.

00:22:25.381 --> 00:22:26.733
I wasn't making fun of you.

00:22:26.999 --> 00:22:29.426
Even a cop can make a mistake, right?

00:22:29.673 --> 00:22:32.210
It's not a mistake.
I just can't stand the sight of blood.

00:22:32.548 --> 00:22:34.188
It makes me dizzy and sick to my stomach.

00:22:34.465 --> 00:22:36.585
And I don't think
that's going to change anytime soon.

00:22:53.619 --> 00:22:54.825
Sir.

00:22:55.833 --> 00:22:58.466
Sir, we caught him with a bottle of booze
during the night patrol.

00:22:58.590 --> 00:23:02.451
This is Vijeesh.
He's a suspect in Justin's case.

00:23:02.631 --> 00:23:04.751
I questioned him,
and it turns out he knew Boban, too.

00:23:05.090 --> 00:23:06.966
He runs a small shop near the school.

00:23:07.673 --> 00:23:11.459
Sir, Justin beat the crap out of me
a month ago

00:23:11.536 --> 00:23:14.825
right in front of the girls
near the school.

00:23:15.173 --> 00:23:16.973
I was so pissed off that
I sent him a message.

00:23:17.298 --> 00:23:19.550
But how am I responsible
if someone else kills him?

00:23:20.340 --> 00:23:21.710
What exactly did you text him?

00:23:22.590 --> 00:23:23.689
We have it noted down, sir.

00:23:24.215 --> 00:23:27.315
"No one has ever dared
to lay a hand on me."

00:23:27.340 --> 00:23:29.590
"Consider yourself
dead, you piece of trash."

00:23:31.590 --> 00:23:32.701
Is that not enough?

00:23:35.423 --> 00:23:37.545
Who did you hire to kill Justin and Boban?

00:23:37.923 --> 00:23:40.400
Maybe Boban was killed by mistake.

00:23:40.548 --> 00:23:43.048
He wasn't a nuisance like Justin.

00:23:43.923 --> 00:23:45.427
How do you know Boban?

00:23:45.881 --> 00:23:48.277
He was a gem of a guy.

00:23:48.575 --> 00:23:51.061
- Everyone in the market knows him.
- Tell me how ♪you-know him.

00:23:51.086 --> 00:23:52.128
Althaf!

00:23:53.423 --> 00:23:54.438
He...

00:23:54.512 --> 00:23:57.066
He treated everyone as equals, sir.

00:23:57.256 --> 00:23:59.899
He'd buy us drinks in the evenings,

00:24:00.090 --> 00:24:02.437
share his booze, and sing songs.

00:24:02.673 --> 00:24:04.593
That's how I ended up
hanging out with his group.

00:24:04.798 --> 00:24:05.906
Hanging out for what?

00:24:06.840 --> 00:24:09.609
Sir, he'd call me
when they ran out of liquor.

00:24:09.840 --> 00:24:11.826
I'd usually have a couple of bottles handy.

00:24:11.965 --> 00:24:13.832
Wait! I don't mean I was selling it...

00:24:17.226 --> 00:24:18.313
Sir.

00:24:19.991 --> 00:24:22.578
Look into this fight he had with Justin
near the school.

00:24:22.881 --> 00:24:24.898
And find out if he peddles weed
like Justin did.

00:24:24.923 --> 00:24:26.398
I don't buy his story, sir.

00:24:26.449 --> 00:24:28.731
Word is, weed is easy to score
from the shops in his area.

00:24:28.756 --> 00:24:29.997
He might be dealing, too.

00:24:30.048 --> 00:24:32.068
Tell Binu to lock him up on suspicion.

00:24:32.123 --> 00:24:33.516
- And, Basheer.
- Sir.

00:24:33.549 --> 00:24:37.015
Get his call records
and tower locations ASAP,

00:24:37.040 --> 00:24:38.362
for the day Boban was killed.

00:24:38.423 --> 00:24:39.686
- We'll deal with the rest later.
- Sir.

00:24:39.710 --> 00:24:41.037
Basheer, come here.

00:24:44.006 --> 00:24:45.615
Hold him at the station, understood?

00:24:56.965 --> 00:24:58.166
Stop, stop, stop.

00:24:59.006 --> 00:25:00.973
Where are you headed so late at night, sir?

00:25:01.715 --> 00:25:03.543
We need to inspect your vehicle.

00:25:07.173 --> 00:25:08.322
What's the matter, Vipin?

00:25:08.881 --> 00:25:09.982
What's going on?

00:25:10.631 --> 00:25:12.677
- Go check the car.
- Yes, sir.

00:25:21.173 --> 00:25:22.379
Where are you going, sir?

00:25:24.298 --> 00:25:25.709
I was just heading over here.

00:25:25.965 --> 00:25:28.384
Is that old lodge at
the junction still open?

00:25:28.840 --> 00:25:30.246
We can check on that later.

00:25:30.340 --> 00:25:32.780
It's not safe to be travelling around here
alone at this hour.

00:25:32.840 --> 00:25:34.158
What brings you here?

00:25:35.256 --> 00:25:37.146
I came to visit an old friend.

00:25:37.340 --> 00:25:38.568
- Sir.
- What?

00:25:39.047 --> 00:25:40.343
Sir... He has a gun.

00:25:43.298 --> 00:25:45.799
I have a permit for self-defence.

00:25:46.756 --> 00:25:48.401
I'm an ex-police officer.

00:25:48.590 --> 00:25:50.938
Name is Swamy.
Plenty of people in the department know me.

00:25:55.548 --> 00:25:57.402
I've been asking around about him.

00:25:57.756 --> 00:26:00.191
I even dropped a message
in the senior officers' WhatsApp group.

00:26:00.215 --> 00:26:02.358
But I didn't expect him
to just show up like this.

00:26:02.923 --> 00:26:04.251
Where is he now?

00:26:04.840 --> 00:26:07.010
I've instructed Sojan
to bring him to the station.

00:26:07.097 --> 00:26:08.398
I'm heading there now.

00:26:08.506 --> 00:26:09.993
Don't take him to the station.

00:26:10.506 --> 00:26:13.377
We can't officially involve him
in the investigation.

00:26:13.631 --> 00:26:15.450
But we need his expertise.

00:26:16.340 --> 00:26:17.620
Here's what you do.

00:26:17.881 --> 00:26:19.966
Isn't Uncle Franci's house empty right now?

00:26:20.548 --> 00:26:22.039
Take him there for the time being.

00:26:23.131 --> 00:26:24.866
We'll figure out the rest in the morning.

00:26:25.506 --> 00:26:26.555
Understood.

00:26:46.506 --> 00:26:48.019
Sir, this is my relative's place.

00:26:48.381 --> 00:26:50.445
I was going to stay here
when I got transferred.

00:26:50.840 --> 00:26:53.412
But my wife and I decided
we prefer living in the city.

00:26:53.465 --> 00:26:54.985
- It's a pretty big house.
- Yeah, it is.

00:26:55.173 --> 00:26:56.348
Sir, you said you already ate.

00:26:56.372 --> 00:26:58.430
But if you need any food,
we can arrange it.

00:26:58.590 --> 00:27:00.841
- No, I'm fine.
- We know restaurants nearby.

00:27:01.090 --> 00:27:02.273
Get some rest, sir.

00:27:02.298 --> 00:27:03.481
We'll be back in the morning.

00:27:03.506 --> 00:27:05.621
We'll talk to Manoj sir
and figure out the rest.

00:27:05.646 --> 00:27:06.949
- Okay, good night, sir.
- Good night, sir.

00:27:06.973 --> 00:27:08.102
- Sir.
- Yeah?

00:27:08.893 --> 00:27:10.059
Yeah, hand it over.

00:27:10.084 --> 00:27:11.093
Sir.

00:27:13.370 --> 00:27:14.979
- Shall I leave, sir?
- Alright.

00:27:45.768 --> 00:27:47.033
Come here, come here.

00:27:47.090 --> 00:27:50.177
What's your name, sweetie?

00:27:50.202 --> 00:27:51.750
Awww!

00:27:54.900 --> 00:27:56.480
Come on. Come.

00:27:57.590 --> 00:27:59.341
You stay right there.

00:28:05.006 --> 00:28:06.510
Two murders in a short span.

00:28:06.715 --> 00:28:08.450
Both executed in a similar way.

00:28:08.881 --> 00:28:09.983
Thank you, sir.

00:28:12.923 --> 00:28:16.234
The fingerprints from both crime scenes
belong to the same person.

00:28:16.340 --> 00:28:18.834
Have you heard anything about this case?

00:28:20.381 --> 00:28:24.225
Ever since I retired,
I purposely ignore such cases.

00:28:24.715 --> 00:28:26.265
Ruins my peace of mind.

00:28:26.631 --> 00:28:28.941
Sorry, we aren't trying to drag you
into this investigation.

00:28:28.965 --> 00:28:31.606
We just want some advice
based on your experience.

00:28:31.756 --> 00:28:33.923
Actually, to help with this case,

00:28:34.131 --> 00:28:36.967
I've been studying the cases you solved
and your methods.

00:28:37.048 --> 00:28:39.725
It's really helpful to have you here
right now.

00:28:39.798 --> 00:28:41.698
I've heard you have a knack,

00:28:41.723 --> 00:28:44.345
for correctly guessing the culprit
right at the crime scene.

00:28:44.423 --> 00:28:46.456
Basically, what we want to know is

00:28:46.480 --> 00:28:49.476
if we are dealing with
a psycho killer here.

00:28:50.048 --> 00:28:53.890
We need your guidance to know
if we're on the right track.

00:28:54.512 --> 00:28:57.148
- This happened quite a long time ago, right?
- Yes, sir.

00:28:57.173 --> 00:28:58.640
These are the kind of insights you get

00:28:58.664 --> 00:29:01.611
only when you visit the crime scene
right after the incident.

00:29:01.673 --> 00:29:03.923
Sir, we have all the
reports and photos here.

00:29:04.340 --> 00:29:06.210
It would be great if you could take a look…

00:29:13.048 --> 00:29:14.955
So, I need to go through all this, right?

00:30:58.175 --> 00:31:00.557
I've heard that
back when you were in service,

00:31:00.582 --> 00:31:03.098
you used black magic to catch culprits.

00:31:05.881 --> 00:31:08.761
In the old days, doctors used to
diagnose and prescribe medicine

00:31:08.786 --> 00:31:12.002
just by looking at a patient
and checking their pulse.

00:31:12.340 --> 00:31:13.634
But think about today.

00:31:13.715 --> 00:31:17.715
They can't even diagnose a severe illness
without an X-ray or a scan.

00:31:18.881 --> 00:31:21.278
We didn't have mobile tower tracking
back then, Althaf.

00:31:21.548 --> 00:31:25.508
And it would take days for forensic
and postmortem reports to arrive.

00:31:26.923 --> 00:31:27.932
Right.

00:31:27.965 --> 00:31:30.467
So, investigators had to use their brains.

00:31:30.840 --> 00:31:34.863
It wasn't black magic or witchcraft,
like you think.

00:31:42.881 --> 00:31:45.826
The killer is shorter than the victims.

00:31:46.756 --> 00:31:50.788
The exact spot and details of the
head injury in the postmortem report

00:31:50.812 --> 00:31:54.006
along with the crime scene evidence,
prove that.

00:31:54.798 --> 00:31:57.098
I'm not sure if you guys noticed that.

00:31:59.756 --> 00:32:02.756
The killer hasn't used any weapons.

00:32:02.923 --> 00:32:05.022
And the victims didn't put up a fight.

00:32:05.090 --> 00:32:06.437
That's what's confusing us.

00:32:06.798 --> 00:32:07.952
Sir, does that mean

00:32:09.984 --> 00:32:13.415
the killer was known to the victims?

00:32:14.631 --> 00:32:16.268
We can't say that for sure.

00:32:16.395 --> 00:32:21.220
What if the killer has an innocent face?
Someone who doesn't look threatening.

00:32:22.298 --> 00:32:25.123
The victims might not have realised
they were in danger.

00:32:25.715 --> 00:32:28.438
Even the killer might not have known
they were about to kill.

00:32:28.811 --> 00:32:31.035
It could have been a
purely impulsive attack.

00:32:39.381 --> 00:32:41.590
For the victims to collapse
from the very first blow,

00:32:41.631 --> 00:32:43.871
the killer's hands must be
incredibly strong. Right, sir?

00:32:44.465 --> 00:32:48.179
That could be a sudden surge of strength
one gets during an unstable mental state.

00:32:48.590 --> 00:32:51.411
From that, we can confirm
the killer is a psycho.

00:32:54.881 --> 00:32:57.480
Do you have anyone
short and innocent-looking

00:32:57.504 --> 00:32:59.131
on your suspect list?

00:33:00.755 --> 00:33:03.034
Yes, sir, we have one guy like that
on the list.

00:33:03.090 --> 00:33:04.893
But he's a dwarf, sir.

00:33:05.526 --> 00:33:07.366
He wouldn't have the strength
to pull this off.

00:33:08.590 --> 00:33:09.930
Think about Boban's case.

00:33:10.048 --> 00:33:12.341
He got out of his car
and walked towards them.

00:33:12.774 --> 00:33:14.833
Justin's body was found
near an electric pole,

00:33:14.858 --> 00:33:17.175
but his bike was parked perfectly
on its stand.

00:33:18.215 --> 00:33:21.157
So, sir, like you mentioned,
an innocent face

00:33:21.181 --> 00:33:24.352
perhaps a woman or a kid?

00:33:24.840 --> 00:33:29.090
Sir, I don't think a woman or a child
would be roaming around at that hour.

00:33:29.896 --> 00:33:33.271
Althaf, we aren't talking about
a normal person here.

00:33:34.473 --> 00:33:37.319
Even so, how could a kid
have that kind of strength?

00:33:38.576 --> 00:33:41.743
What if it's an athlete?
Someone who plays badminton or tennis.

00:33:42.006 --> 00:33:44.048
Or a kid who plays cricket.

00:33:44.465 --> 00:33:47.385
The power needed to hit a six is more
than enough to smash someone's head.

00:33:48.631 --> 00:33:50.715
By the way, these are just my assumptions.

00:33:51.131 --> 00:33:52.524
Don't discard any of your own findings.

00:33:52.548 --> 00:33:54.467
Just keep these points in mind
while you investigate.

00:33:54.491 --> 00:33:55.694
You might get a solid lead.

00:34:39.256 --> 00:34:42.590
We went through all the case files involving
women and kids in our jurisdiction.

00:34:43.048 --> 00:34:46.044
We've requested them to hand over
any suspicious files.

00:34:46.798 --> 00:34:48.690
Didn't you say you found something?

00:34:49.266 --> 00:34:53.731
I followed Swamy's instinct that
the killer could be a cricketer.

00:34:54.006 --> 00:34:55.881
It's from a case Binu handled.

00:34:56.298 --> 00:34:59.543
A kid was beaten up by four others
at a cricket ground.

00:35:00.048 --> 00:35:01.407
Did you get the details?

00:35:01.631 --> 00:35:04.631
Some politicians got involved
and settled it off the books.

00:35:05.048 --> 00:35:07.440
But Binu says they are troublemakers.

00:35:07.465 --> 00:35:10.027
There is drug dealing happening in schools,

00:35:10.052 --> 00:35:11.734
and he says these kids are involved.

00:35:11.840 --> 00:35:13.821
Then gather all their details immediately.

00:35:13.965 --> 00:35:15.461
Already done, sir.

00:35:16.465 --> 00:35:18.355
These kids have a connection to Justin.

00:35:18.505 --> 00:35:22.006
This is an Instagram post from
one of them, Amit. Take a look.

00:35:33.298 --> 00:35:35.933
Sir, these four kids play cricket together.

00:35:36.246 --> 00:35:41.681
And just like you said,
they're all shorter than the victims.

00:35:42.631 --> 00:35:45.777
At first glance, they look pretty innocent
in these photos too.

00:35:46.280 --> 00:35:49.330
Although most kids their age do.

00:35:50.256 --> 00:35:54.413
We found out these kids
are definitely linked to Justin.

00:35:55.006 --> 00:35:58.413
Also, Boban is a distant relative
of one of them.

00:35:58.673 --> 00:36:00.372
We're looking into that as well.

00:36:00.923 --> 00:36:03.858
Justin was using them as carriers
to peddle weed in schools.

00:36:03.883 --> 00:36:05.305
That's the information we got.

00:36:06.131 --> 00:36:07.682
Since they're minors,

00:36:07.706 --> 00:36:11.713
Manoj sir instructed us to bring them in
only if we have solid evidence.

00:36:11.965 --> 00:36:13.193
What do you think, sir?

00:36:37.881 --> 00:36:39.198
The killer isn't one of them.

00:36:39.715 --> 00:36:41.851
Sir, how can you be so sure?

00:36:43.590 --> 00:36:46.489
That is exactly the difference
between you and me.

00:36:49.923 --> 00:36:52.707
We are looking for a killer
who operates entirely alone.

00:36:53.006 --> 00:36:57.624
If we were looking for a gang of kids
planning a murder together,

00:36:57.649 --> 00:36:59.318
you would have caught them easily.

00:36:59.381 --> 00:37:00.621
That's not my point, sir.

00:37:00.673 --> 00:37:03.684
What if drugs turned one of them
into a killer?

00:37:04.131 --> 00:37:07.429
Violent video games, thriller web series,
hanging out with criminals

00:37:07.590 --> 00:37:09.363
all of this can mess with a kid's mind.

00:37:12.381 --> 00:37:17.242
Contrary to what you think,
a person doesn't just wake up one day

00:37:17.266 --> 00:37:19.782
as a psycho serial killer.

00:37:20.806 --> 00:37:23.523
They are born with that instinct.

00:37:25.006 --> 00:37:28.881
Add a troubled childhood, early trauma,

00:37:29.548 --> 00:37:32.819
with no one to love or care for them…

00:37:33.673 --> 00:37:35.400
They become lonely and detached…

00:37:36.465 --> 00:37:39.465
Slowly evolving into a psychopathic killer.

00:37:42.465 --> 00:37:43.854
Understand?

00:37:44.568 --> 00:37:45.648
That's how it works.

00:37:55.756 --> 00:37:59.325
The first murder usually has
a clear motive.

00:38:00.215 --> 00:38:02.055
But then they start enjoying the thrill of it.

00:38:02.590 --> 00:38:04.467
That's when they start killing
again and again.

00:38:05.381 --> 00:38:07.900
These kids are from affluent families.
They live comfortably.

00:38:08.173 --> 00:38:10.444
They haven't faced those kinds of
dark circumstances.

00:38:11.381 --> 00:38:14.374
What about the kid who was beaten up
by them at the cricket ground?

00:38:14.506 --> 00:38:16.733
Did you look into him? Is he happy?

00:38:18.653 --> 00:38:20.976
After that incident,
he was transferred to another school.

00:38:21.001 --> 00:38:22.481
He doesn't live in this town anymore.

00:38:23.798 --> 00:38:25.840
He's the one you need to question first.

00:38:26.506 --> 00:38:28.860
See if your profile matches him.

00:38:29.506 --> 00:38:31.513
He's the one who took the beating, right?

00:38:45.603 --> 00:38:46.750
What's the matter?

00:38:47.173 --> 00:38:49.131
Sir, we came to see the Circle Inspector.

00:38:49.371 --> 00:38:50.591
Please wait there.

00:39:20.735 --> 00:39:21.801
Sir.

00:39:23.756 --> 00:39:25.191
- Ask them to wait inside.
- Okay, sir.

00:39:25.215 --> 00:39:26.414
I'll be right there.

00:39:30.410 --> 00:39:33.315
Sir, the boy's father is Vinayan.

00:39:33.340 --> 00:39:34.725
He used to be a carpenter.

00:39:34.798 --> 00:39:36.979
According to the Neighbors,
he doesn't work anymore,

00:39:37.004 --> 00:39:38.824
and just stays at home all day.

00:39:39.090 --> 00:39:41.201
The mother's name is Kavitha.

00:39:41.340 --> 00:39:43.965
She is an insurance agent.

00:39:44.048 --> 00:39:47.144
She also works at a small embroidery unit.

00:39:47.631 --> 00:39:49.468
Adityan is their only son.

00:39:49.715 --> 00:39:51.865
That's all the background we have.

00:39:52.215 --> 00:39:53.611
His mother is waiting outside.

00:39:54.006 --> 00:39:56.100
Keep it friendly and try to get
maximum info from them.

00:39:56.124 --> 00:39:57.386
Okay, sir.

00:40:22.923 --> 00:40:25.301
I have a soft spot for cricket.

00:40:27.215 --> 00:40:28.623
You are Adityan, right?

00:40:28.807 --> 00:40:29.915
Hello.

00:40:31.631 --> 00:40:33.263
Batsman or bowler?

00:40:34.340 --> 00:40:35.785
Why was I called here?

00:40:37.298 --> 00:40:39.011
I heard you're a great cricket player.

00:40:39.173 --> 00:40:40.791
Just thought I'd meet you.

00:40:44.482 --> 00:40:46.264
Hey, don't be so quiet.

00:40:46.288 --> 00:40:48.415
Say something. Come on.

00:40:48.524 --> 00:40:49.812
My mother has to go to work, sir.

00:40:49.836 --> 00:40:51.477
We've been waiting here for a long time.

00:40:51.881 --> 00:40:54.189
I heard your dad is unemployed.

00:40:54.384 --> 00:40:56.176
You could have just come with him.

00:40:57.215 --> 00:41:00.381
The mess he made at the station last time
hasn't been resolved yet.

00:41:01.307 --> 00:41:02.940
I'm aware of that incident.

00:41:03.173 --> 00:41:04.886
Those other kids beat you up, right?

00:41:07.013 --> 00:41:09.191
What happened on that day?

00:41:10.923 --> 00:41:12.923
That's in the past.

00:41:14.043 --> 00:41:18.126
But we need to know everything
about you right now.

00:41:18.610 --> 00:41:20.071
That's why you're here.

00:41:25.340 --> 00:41:27.161
You didn't answer my question.

00:41:27.881 --> 00:41:29.303
Batsman or bowler?

00:41:29.756 --> 00:41:31.998
Both. I'm the team's fast bowler.

00:41:38.963 --> 00:41:40.547
Adi, stop it.

00:41:41.338 --> 00:41:43.172
You should speak respectfully to your dad.

00:41:43.838 --> 00:41:44.838
Dad, my foot!

00:41:44.880 --> 00:41:46.731
Is he of any use to anyone?

00:41:46.991 --> 00:41:48.688
I'm getting nowhere with my studies.

00:41:48.713 --> 00:41:50.179
I want to play cricket.

00:41:50.213 --> 00:41:51.981
I'm definitely going for training
when it starts.

00:41:52.005 --> 00:41:53.679
You have to give me the money for it.

00:41:53.880 --> 00:41:56.627
What are you saying?
How much money do you need?

00:41:56.651 --> 00:41:59.178
Tell me, how much does a cricket kit cost?
Huh?

00:41:59.630 --> 00:42:02.910
There are plenty of people in this world
living peacefully without playing cricket.

00:42:03.547 --> 00:42:05.387
What's the big deal if you don't play?

00:42:06.630 --> 00:42:08.437
Go inside.

00:42:10.380 --> 00:42:13.400
I don't plan on letting my son
sit idle at home like you.

00:42:14.209 --> 00:42:15.798
Just remember that.

00:43:18.983 --> 00:43:20.905
"Fixed deposit interest rates
slashed by 1.3%."

00:43:20.929 --> 00:43:22.897
"8.5% for senior citizens. 8% for others."

00:43:33.610 --> 00:43:35.451
- Is he back?
- He came back and went out again.

00:43:36.338 --> 00:43:37.532
Kavitha,

00:43:38.338 --> 00:43:42.499
the interest on our treasury deposit
has dropped by 1.3%.

00:43:42.547 --> 00:43:46.983
That means our monthly income
is going to take a hit.

00:43:47.329 --> 00:43:50.397
You're bringing this up because I sent him
for cricket coaching, right?

00:43:50.422 --> 00:43:53.647
If I start the same, things will get ugly.

00:43:53.672 --> 00:43:56.061
The money in the bank is from
selling my jewellery.

00:43:56.205 --> 00:43:57.894
It's not your hard-earned money.

00:43:58.297 --> 00:44:00.866
Let him become a successful cricketer.

00:44:00.891 --> 00:44:02.680
That's the only way our lives will improve.

00:44:03.979 --> 00:44:05.192
But...

00:44:05.630 --> 00:44:06.960
What's wrong with our lives right now?

00:44:06.984 --> 00:44:08.418
Oh yeah, no problems at all!

00:44:08.588 --> 00:44:13.022
Everyone who worked with you owns
timber mills and furniture showrooms now.

00:44:13.053 --> 00:44:16.260
They drive around in luxury cars.
And look at us.

00:44:17.297 --> 00:44:18.881
But it's just the three of us.

00:44:19.047 --> 00:44:22.213
Isn't a bike enough for us to get around?

00:44:23.005 --> 00:44:25.547
Bike! Fine, go and pick him up.

00:44:25.736 --> 00:44:27.230
Otherwise, he'll take an auto.

00:44:27.255 --> 00:44:29.763
And then you'll complain
about that expense too.

00:44:29.787 --> 00:44:30.875
Go now.

00:45:22.735 --> 00:45:24.061
Hey, move. Get out of the way.

00:45:28.880 --> 00:45:30.303
Stop right there!

00:45:34.548 --> 00:45:35.929
Dad, start the bike!

00:45:36.172 --> 00:45:37.588
Stop right there!

00:45:38.880 --> 00:45:40.005
Go faster, Dad. Faster!

00:45:40.030 --> 00:45:41.109
Catch them!

00:45:41.134 --> 00:45:43.345
- Go faster, Dad. Faster!
- Who are these guys?

00:45:43.370 --> 00:45:45.438
Hurry up, Dad! Hurry!

00:46:40.838 --> 00:46:42.020
Come on.

00:46:42.672 --> 00:46:43.946
Get off.

00:46:46.547 --> 00:46:48.088
- Move.
- Bring them here.

00:46:56.380 --> 00:46:58.082
Don't stop. Keep walking!

00:47:06.213 --> 00:47:07.452
Whose bag is this?

00:47:07.588 --> 00:47:08.752
Not ours, sir.

00:47:08.797 --> 00:47:10.527
Then how did it end up in your cricket kit?

00:47:10.880 --> 00:47:12.184
I don't know, sir.

00:47:12.422 --> 00:47:14.351
Did it magically appear in the kit
on its own?

00:47:16.463 --> 00:47:18.596
- Who is he?
- My friend, sir.

00:47:19.630 --> 00:47:20.862
Where does he live?

00:47:20.922 --> 00:47:22.217
Near the market, sir.

00:47:22.255 --> 00:47:24.522
Why are you shaking? Stand straight.

00:47:24.547 --> 00:47:25.994
Hold on. Stop writing.

00:47:26.172 --> 00:47:28.292
This is a drug case. Go wait outside.

00:47:28.317 --> 00:47:30.458
Look at him! Is he your ringleader?

00:47:30.547 --> 00:47:31.784
Come here.

00:47:52.130 --> 00:47:54.461
Why on earth did you bring your son here?

00:47:54.713 --> 00:47:57.353
Do you have any idea how hard it is
to get out of a mess like this?

00:48:03.753 --> 00:48:05.981
Someone was selling illegal booze
near my nephew's place.

00:48:06.005 --> 00:48:08.405
He begged them to stop.
They didn't listen.

00:48:08.699 --> 00:48:10.824
He filed a police complaint.

00:48:10.948 --> 00:48:13.148
The police filed a case
and destroyed all the booze.

00:48:13.213 --> 00:48:15.933
You know what happened next?
The case just vanished after a few days.

00:48:16.104 --> 00:48:18.396
No one was arrested or charged.

00:48:18.747 --> 00:48:20.707
The police and the bootleggers
were hand in glove.

00:48:20.760 --> 00:48:22.593
My nephew couldn't live there anymore.

00:48:23.073 --> 00:48:26.062
His daughter was preparing
for her medical entrance.

00:48:26.087 --> 00:48:27.808
But they had to sell their land
for pennies,

00:48:27.832 --> 00:48:29.628
and flee to Nagercoil to save their lives.

00:48:29.652 --> 00:48:32.652
The girl who wanted to be a doctor
is working on a farm now.

00:48:37.147 --> 00:48:38.522
These politicians

00:48:38.593 --> 00:48:40.698
they bring the police
and the drug dealers together.

00:48:40.722 --> 00:48:43.003
In the end, it's common people
like you and me who suffer.

00:49:02.221 --> 00:49:03.672
Come on, man.

00:49:04.338 --> 00:49:05.935
- What happened?
- What happened to him?

00:49:05.963 --> 00:49:07.534
They've taken him to the hospital.

00:49:08.005 --> 00:49:09.385
Dad is waiting outside. Let me...

00:49:09.762 --> 00:49:10.907
Wait.

00:49:14.102 --> 00:49:15.334
Get on.

00:49:16.838 --> 00:49:19.505
You think you can just
bust my friend's head open and walk away?

00:49:20.838 --> 00:49:25.588
I'm letting you go for now
only because we're at the police station.

00:49:26.505 --> 00:49:29.505
I'll come to your house and settle this.

00:49:40.336 --> 00:49:41.711
Do you know him?

00:49:42.134 --> 00:49:43.218
No.

00:49:45.088 --> 00:49:46.648
- Have you ever seen him?
- No, I haven't.

00:49:49.963 --> 00:49:51.630
He wouldn't lie, sir.

00:49:53.338 --> 00:49:55.613
You sent him to
your sister's place in Kayamkulam

00:49:55.638 --> 00:49:57.617
on the very day of the incident.

00:49:57.797 --> 00:50:01.131
Is this his first time back since then?

00:50:01.156 --> 00:50:02.848
Or has he visited before?

00:50:06.130 --> 00:50:07.438
What is there to think about?

00:50:07.463 --> 00:50:09.223
Wouldn't you know if
your own son came home?

00:50:09.338 --> 00:50:11.907
It's not that, madam. He came twice.

00:50:12.005 --> 00:50:13.421
But he didn't come to the house.

00:50:13.505 --> 00:50:15.502
He came for his cricket matches.

00:50:15.880 --> 00:50:17.928
He met me at work.

00:50:18.172 --> 00:50:19.556
What date was that?

00:50:20.954 --> 00:50:22.580
The date...

00:50:22.838 --> 00:50:25.281
Madam, I don't remember the exact date.

00:50:25.338 --> 00:50:26.803
It was sometime last month.

00:50:28.088 --> 00:50:30.147
The first match got cancelled
because of a death.

00:50:30.172 --> 00:50:32.532
Madam, don't you remember?
A boy was murdered on the street.

00:50:32.672 --> 00:50:33.912
He arrived the day before that.

00:50:36.963 --> 00:50:40.429
Why did he visit only his mother
without letting his dad know?

00:50:43.463 --> 00:50:44.771
Hi, sis.

00:50:44.963 --> 00:50:47.163
You didn't need to take Adityan
to your place right now.

00:50:47.338 --> 00:50:50.230
It was just a petty fight
between the kids at the playground.

00:50:50.672 --> 00:50:52.954
And you know
how Vinayan reacts to these things.

00:50:58.338 --> 00:51:00.699
Listen, Adityan hasn't eaten anything.

00:51:00.880 --> 00:51:02.499
Please call me as soon as he gets there.

00:51:05.963 --> 00:51:07.740
I'll call you back. Vinayan is here.

00:51:18.088 --> 00:51:19.088
- What is it?
- Go inside.

00:51:21.005 --> 00:51:22.214
Who are those guys?

00:51:23.801 --> 00:51:24.838
Just get inside.

00:51:24.963 --> 00:51:26.745
You hid him, huh?!

00:51:27.756 --> 00:51:28.813
Come on, get inside.

00:51:28.838 --> 00:51:30.162
Come out here!

00:51:34.088 --> 00:51:35.352
Come out!

00:51:35.377 --> 00:51:36.327
Get in!

00:51:36.352 --> 00:51:37.644
Throw it at his head.

00:51:38.047 --> 00:51:39.410
Come out!

00:51:40.880 --> 00:51:42.238
We'll deal with you later.

00:51:52.880 --> 00:51:54.426
I told Binu sir everything.

00:51:54.755 --> 00:51:55.987
But there's a problem.

00:51:56.505 --> 00:51:59.918
All the kids involved in that case
are from rich families.

00:52:00.088 --> 00:52:02.648
That's why the Sub-Inspector
got involved and settled the matter.

00:52:02.922 --> 00:52:04.987
Binu sir won't be able to reopen that case.

00:52:06.047 --> 00:52:08.159
But he suggested something else we can do.

00:52:08.777 --> 00:52:12.146
Stating that local goons are harassing you,
and you need police protection,

00:52:12.171 --> 00:52:14.709
write a new petition
and take it to the Circle Inspector.

00:52:14.755 --> 00:52:16.436
Binu sir has promised to help us out.

00:52:20.297 --> 00:52:22.878
But think twice before you make a decision.

00:52:25.505 --> 00:52:30.145
I'm afraid they might attack me
to get back at my son.

00:52:31.463 --> 00:52:34.415
I haven't had a peaceful night's sleep
in days.

00:52:36.630 --> 00:52:38.038
I will file the petition.

00:52:38.713 --> 00:52:41.172
Having the police on my side
will give me some courage.

00:52:42.088 --> 00:52:43.102
Alright.

00:52:48.748 --> 00:52:53.748
'I humbly request you
to grant me police protection.'

00:52:58.848 --> 00:52:59.875
Yes, sir?

00:52:59.900 --> 00:53:02.649
Hey, that Vinayan case
has landed back on our desk.

00:53:02.857 --> 00:53:04.657
Didn't we settle that case
out of the station?

00:53:04.804 --> 00:53:07.144
Is that the case involving those kids, sir?

00:53:07.706 --> 00:53:09.499
We already settled it, sir.

00:53:09.810 --> 00:53:10.883
It was all sorted out.

00:53:10.908 --> 00:53:12.336
But he's come back now!

00:53:12.382 --> 00:53:14.036
I'll go and look into it, sir.

00:53:14.095 --> 00:53:15.262
Has he left?

00:53:15.287 --> 00:53:17.095
No. Let me have a word with him.

00:53:17.713 --> 00:53:18.713
Alright.

00:53:18.797 --> 00:53:19.838
Hey!

00:53:20.505 --> 00:53:21.724
What are you doing?

00:53:22.110 --> 00:53:23.606
How dare you touch the files
on my desk?

00:53:23.630 --> 00:53:24.963
Get up! Get up!

00:53:25.213 --> 00:53:26.550
Get out!

00:53:29.130 --> 00:53:30.586
I said, get out.

00:53:40.713 --> 00:53:42.949
Why is my photo in a police file?

00:53:43.380 --> 00:53:44.539
It must be someone else.

00:53:44.588 --> 00:53:45.879
You must have been mistaken.

00:53:47.880 --> 00:53:49.500
I saw it with my own eyes, Kavitha.

00:54:06.463 --> 00:54:07.834
Have you noticed?

00:54:08.130 --> 00:54:10.348
Those goons haven't bothered us
for the last two days.

00:54:12.630 --> 00:54:14.468
That file probably has my photo in it too.

00:54:15.672 --> 00:54:18.154
From now on, it's the police
who will be harassing us.

00:54:18.713 --> 00:54:20.473
You're worried about
those boys, aren't you?

00:54:20.755 --> 00:54:23.066
Adi must have taken care of them.

00:54:23.630 --> 00:54:25.034
They won't come around here again.

00:54:25.213 --> 00:54:27.461
Just eat your dinner and go to sleep.

00:54:28.393 --> 00:54:31.152
If goons come after us,
we can at least complain to the police.

00:54:31.255 --> 00:54:33.652
If the police are after us,
who do we complain to?

00:54:34.088 --> 00:54:35.480
They can frame us for anything,

00:54:35.505 --> 00:54:37.873
lock us up, and beat us to a pulp.

00:54:38.547 --> 00:54:40.992
You know how many people they've killed
like that in the past.

00:54:45.838 --> 00:54:47.856
We don't have any other way out.

00:54:49.213 --> 00:54:50.563
Let's just die.

00:54:51.797 --> 00:54:53.023
Brilliant idea! Let's just die.

00:54:53.047 --> 00:54:55.293
It's better than living this pathetic life.

00:54:55.797 --> 00:54:58.353
This is exactly how
the story of every coward ends.

00:54:59.299 --> 00:55:01.573
If only you had a fraction of
your son's courage!

00:55:21.463 --> 00:55:23.021
What about our son?

00:55:23.713 --> 00:55:24.950
What about him?

00:55:27.380 --> 00:55:30.850
Even if we die,
the police might still catch him.

00:55:35.088 --> 00:55:36.975
He is not a coward like you.

00:55:37.588 --> 00:55:39.282
He is a brave boy.

00:55:39.672 --> 00:55:41.355
If you ask him to die with you,

00:55:41.380 --> 00:55:43.060
he'd probably just kill you and go to jail.

00:55:43.130 --> 00:55:45.027
But we have to do something about him…

00:55:45.505 --> 00:55:46.753
Here's what we'll do.

00:55:46.963 --> 00:55:48.499
Let's call him home.

00:55:48.630 --> 00:55:52.039
And we'll poison his milk or ice cream.

00:55:52.505 --> 00:55:53.825
After that, we'll kill ourselves.

00:55:54.255 --> 00:55:56.269
Now, go and get some milk.

00:55:56.422 --> 00:55:58.434
Get two packets.
There's no point in saving money now.

00:55:58.458 --> 00:55:59.938
Let's have a nice, creamy cup of tea.

00:56:00.088 --> 00:56:01.634
We're going to die anyway.

00:56:01.922 --> 00:56:04.264
We don't have to worry about the interest.

00:56:09.213 --> 00:56:10.620
Here's your tea.

00:56:16.056 --> 00:56:17.242
Look at him.

00:56:17.266 --> 00:56:18.760
It's hilarious.

00:56:27.630 --> 00:56:28.676
See?

00:56:33.005 --> 00:56:36.190
Now he's going to hand me exactly 23 rupees
and ask for one packet of milk.

00:56:36.215 --> 00:56:37.410
Just wait and watch.

00:56:39.831 --> 00:56:41.058
Two packets of milk.

00:56:41.172 --> 00:56:42.286
Well, this is a surprise.

00:56:42.311 --> 00:56:44.019
Expecting guests?

00:56:44.313 --> 00:56:46.806
Want me to give you some banana fritters
for the change?

00:56:47.088 --> 00:56:48.813
No. Just give me some ice cream.

00:56:48.838 --> 00:56:50.505
Ice cream?

00:56:51.069 --> 00:56:52.269
Here you go.

00:57:33.713 --> 00:57:36.338
Kavitha has been an insurance agent
for the last four years, sir.

00:57:36.729 --> 00:57:37.772
Okay.

00:57:37.910 --> 00:57:40.508
If this boy is the killer,
I feel terrible for this woman.

00:57:41.838 --> 00:57:43.434
That boy is completely lying.

00:57:43.766 --> 00:57:46.246
Do you think the woman is
trying to cover for him?

00:57:46.496 --> 00:57:49.612
No, sir. But given how her husband is,

00:57:49.637 --> 00:57:52.231
she probably tried to raise her son
to be courageous.

00:57:52.493 --> 00:57:54.535
So she might just support him
no matter what.

00:57:54.838 --> 00:57:57.521
She probably can't even imagine him
doing something like this.

00:58:08.713 --> 00:58:11.963
Why are you keeping me here
for no reason? Can I leave?

00:58:12.100 --> 00:58:13.978
Who said there's no reason?

00:58:15.421 --> 00:58:16.456
Sit down.

00:58:18.444 --> 00:58:19.512
Sit.

00:58:25.146 --> 00:58:26.327
Come on.

00:58:27.630 --> 00:58:29.160
Beat me first.

00:58:52.963 --> 00:58:54.192
Based on what you've told me,

00:58:54.239 --> 00:58:55.405
if he wanted to kill someone,

00:58:55.430 --> 00:58:58.423
he has the nerve to pick up a weapon,
look them in the eye, and kill them.

00:59:00.804 --> 00:59:02.490
The guy you're looking for

00:59:02.729 --> 00:59:03.896
it's not him.

01:01:47.102 --> 01:01:49.568
All six cases Swamy sir handled
were extremely complicated.

01:01:49.935 --> 01:01:51.668
But he solved all of them in record time.

01:01:53.060 --> 01:01:56.060
Anyone who solves such cases with ease
has to be a little crazy themselves.

01:01:56.560 --> 01:01:58.646
I really don't think you are crazy enough.

01:01:59.352 --> 01:02:01.144
Maybe that's why you're taking so long.

01:02:01.519 --> 01:02:04.199
Even a simple Google search on
serial killers will drive you insane.

01:02:04.464 --> 01:02:06.465
The ones who kill 10 people, 250 people,

01:02:06.490 --> 01:02:09.078
the ones who target only women,
doctors who kill their patients,

01:02:09.102 --> 01:02:10.310
and worst of all,

01:02:10.334 --> 01:02:12.852
those who kidnap, assault,
and murder children. Sickening.

01:02:15.019 --> 01:02:16.435
Food is ready.

01:02:16.894 --> 01:02:18.102
Okay, thank you.

01:02:21.047 --> 01:02:23.189
Serial killers don't necessarily
have to kill people

01:02:23.213 --> 01:02:24.727
at regular intervals, do they?

01:02:25.302 --> 01:02:26.552
Even they might take a break.

01:02:27.352 --> 01:02:28.725
Christy, you know something?

01:02:28.852 --> 01:02:32.477
In Europe, a 65-year-old man
was arrested for murder.

01:02:32.852 --> 01:02:35.810
It brought to light 9 other murders
he committed 20 years ago.

01:02:43.019 --> 01:02:46.019
In our case, there's no sign
of that kind of waiting or planning.

01:02:47.019 --> 01:02:51.352
I've read about two classifications:
"act-focused" and "process-focused."

01:02:52.227 --> 01:02:55.727
This case looks "act-focused" to me.

01:02:56.477 --> 01:02:57.935
Let me explain "act-focused."

01:02:58.185 --> 01:03:00.748
While driving,
you might get a sudden urge

01:03:00.772 --> 01:03:02.144
to ram the car in front of you.

01:03:02.269 --> 01:03:03.950
Or if you have a stone in your hand,

01:03:03.974 --> 01:03:06.294
you might feel the urge to
smash it against someone's head.

01:03:06.521 --> 01:03:07.641
Or say

01:03:08.477 --> 01:03:11.090
you're holding this stick.

01:03:11.114 --> 01:03:13.727
You just feel like smashing that glass.

01:03:15.435 --> 01:03:16.910
We all get these fleeting thoughts.

01:03:16.934 --> 01:03:19.144
But we don't act on them,
because we are sane.

01:03:20.185 --> 01:03:21.394
From what I've gathered

01:03:25.102 --> 01:03:27.685
these killers revisit the
crime scenes over and over again.

01:03:27.935 --> 01:03:30.921
They replay the entire episode
scene-by-scene in their heads.

01:03:32.060 --> 01:03:34.665
There's another type who seek out
deserted places where no one

01:03:34.689 --> 01:03:37.102
else goes, and just sit there
all alone… for hours.

01:03:38.477 --> 01:03:40.977
It could even be the crime scene
of some other killer.

01:03:41.185 --> 01:03:42.591
Or it could be a cemetery.

01:03:43.685 --> 01:03:47.102
Experts say they get a kind of orgasm
out of it.

01:03:47.269 --> 01:03:49.799
In their suppressed mental state,

01:03:49.823 --> 01:03:54.477
if it makes them feel superior,
it gives them a high.

01:04:08.310 --> 01:04:09.870
You're losing track of time these days.

01:04:09.940 --> 01:04:11.196
Don't you want to eat?

01:04:12.769 --> 01:04:13.855
Come on.

01:04:38.793 --> 01:04:39.913
Haven't you left yet?

01:04:44.560 --> 01:04:45.886
I asked, haven't you left?

01:04:46.769 --> 01:04:47.849
Where is he supposed to go?

01:04:48.102 --> 01:04:49.269
What's your problem, Dad?

01:04:50.019 --> 01:04:51.185
Isn't this my house too?

01:04:51.519 --> 01:04:52.685
I am not going anywhere.

01:04:55.894 --> 01:04:57.195
Please make him understand.

01:04:57.219 --> 01:04:58.907
It's better for him to stay away from here.

01:04:59.144 --> 01:05:01.310
The police ordered him not to leave town.

01:05:01.477 --> 01:05:03.310
Even if the police hadn't said that,

01:05:03.810 --> 01:05:05.685
Dad is just trying to
scare me for no reason.

01:05:06.810 --> 01:05:08.990
I am starting my cricket coaching
tomorrow.

01:05:09.019 --> 01:05:11.102
I've somehow managed to settle
all those old grudges.

01:05:11.560 --> 01:05:13.146
They are all good friends of mine now.

01:05:13.394 --> 01:05:15.411
It won't end well if
he stays here, I'm warning you.

01:05:15.435 --> 01:05:17.535
If you're so uncomfortable,
why don't you just leave?

01:05:17.769 --> 01:05:19.589
- Adi.
- Anyway, this is my mom's house.

01:05:19.727 --> 01:05:21.235
Adi, stop. That's enough.

01:05:22.435 --> 01:05:25.977
He has teamed up with Amit and is
planning to start a small business.

01:05:27.560 --> 01:05:29.746
He'll earn the money
he needs for cricket on his own.

01:05:30.185 --> 01:05:31.519
Why are you getting so worked up?

01:05:34.352 --> 01:05:35.545
Just eat.

01:06:03.852 --> 01:06:05.394
Take a break, Christy.

01:06:06.185 --> 01:06:09.269
Just take your mind off duty
and this case for a bit, and try to sleep.

01:06:09.727 --> 01:06:11.047
You can handle the rest tomorrow.

01:06:19.102 --> 01:06:20.135
Yes, brother.

01:06:20.238 --> 01:06:21.780
I have a doubt.

01:06:22.227 --> 01:06:24.894
What makes you think
the psycho is a local?

01:06:25.560 --> 01:06:28.160
Someone from outside could have
come here and committed the crime.

01:06:28.769 --> 01:06:31.227
While we are beefing up
patrols around here,

01:06:31.727 --> 01:06:33.927
what if he kills someone
in a completely different area?

01:06:34.019 --> 01:06:36.952
People will say we were careless
even when we knew it was a serial killer.

01:06:36.977 --> 01:06:38.840
Psychos like this never commit

01:06:38.865 --> 01:06:42.157
their first crime too close to,
or too far from, their own home.

01:06:42.269 --> 01:06:43.620
There are studies confirming this.

01:06:43.644 --> 01:06:45.560
Because we stepped up the night patrols,

01:06:45.644 --> 01:06:47.078
the killer is unable to step outside.

01:06:47.102 --> 01:06:49.981
That's exactly why no new murders
are being reported.

01:06:50.019 --> 01:06:51.166
He is right here in this town.

01:06:51.190 --> 01:06:53.630
Bullshit! Do these killers have
some sort of rulebook or what?

01:06:53.810 --> 01:06:56.179
With dos and don'ts?

01:06:57.185 --> 01:07:02.144
Your method of investigating by
reading novels is making me nervous.

01:07:04.769 --> 01:07:06.475
Do one thing.

01:07:06.500 --> 01:07:08.931
Hold a press meet tomorrow,
and spread fear over the public.

01:07:09.141 --> 01:07:10.661
Please don't confuse me.

01:07:11.102 --> 01:07:13.853
I will report to the office tomorrow, okay?

01:07:13.877 --> 01:07:14.977
Good night.

01:08:25.977 --> 01:08:26.977
Should I come there now?

01:08:27.227 --> 01:08:28.352
No, don't do that, man.

01:08:29.060 --> 01:08:31.140
The place under the bridge
is swarming with cops.

01:08:31.560 --> 01:08:33.180
I'll send the stuff to your place.

01:08:33.310 --> 01:08:35.269
Is it? Alright then.

01:09:38.185 --> 01:09:39.465
Hello.

01:09:39.852 --> 01:09:42.894
Sir, strictly based on your intuition,
please answer my question.

01:09:43.477 --> 01:09:45.877
Sir, do you honestly think
I am capable of solving this case?

01:09:47.102 --> 01:09:48.228
What happened?

01:09:48.310 --> 01:09:51.019
If a more experienced officer
were investigating this

01:09:51.435 --> 01:09:53.269
they might have solved it by now.

01:09:53.602 --> 01:09:57.310
At this point... aren't we just playing
with innocent people's lives?

01:09:58.727 --> 01:10:00.927
You need to find the thrill
in the investigation itself.

01:10:01.435 --> 01:10:02.769
You have to look at it that way.

01:10:03.394 --> 01:10:04.947
Treat it like a mind game.

01:10:05.560 --> 01:10:07.720
You have to enjoy the process
in order to win the game.

01:10:09.185 --> 01:10:12.435
You aren't finding that thrill
in this case, are you?

01:10:13.339 --> 01:10:15.411
Every time I manage to dig up a clue

01:10:15.436 --> 01:10:17.558
you shoot it down with
a different perspective.

01:10:17.806 --> 01:10:19.833
You haven't even given me
a strong hint so far.

01:10:20.727 --> 01:10:22.607
No one is going give you hints, Christy.

01:10:22.727 --> 01:10:25.379
The clues might be right in front of us.
We're just missing them.

01:10:27.102 --> 01:10:29.644
The more I dig into this,
the more complicated it gets.

01:10:30.894 --> 01:10:33.852
I feel like... I've hit a dead end
with this investigation.

01:10:34.450 --> 01:10:37.138
I have a strong feeling that
the culprit is very close.

01:10:37.163 --> 01:10:38.937
You will find him. I will help you too.

01:10:38.961 --> 01:10:40.661
Just keep moving forward
without losing hope.

01:10:40.685 --> 01:10:42.175
Okay, sir.

01:10:43.144 --> 01:10:44.625
How did it die?

01:10:44.810 --> 01:10:46.310
It was playing around here.

01:10:46.977 --> 01:10:48.477
I found it dead this morning.

01:10:49.727 --> 01:10:51.227
If I don't bury it right away

01:10:51.310 --> 01:10:53.071
those so-called
animal lovers will show up

01:10:53.096 --> 01:10:54.296
and accuse me of killing it.

01:10:54.853 --> 01:10:56.207
I'm not joking, sir.

01:10:56.232 --> 01:10:58.482
Last month,
a dog was found dead near my shop.

01:10:58.506 --> 01:10:59.935
Probably got run over by a vehicle.

01:11:00.560 --> 01:11:01.868
Those "blogger kids" showed up

01:11:01.892 --> 01:11:04.886
and posted it on the internet
claiming it was a murder.

01:11:12.769 --> 01:11:14.935
Where is your shop? What do you do?

01:11:16.602 --> 01:11:17.977
Nothing big, sir.

01:11:18.352 --> 01:11:21.310
I run a milk booth at Koonanmukku.

01:11:22.144 --> 01:11:24.310
My banana fritters are pretty famous.

01:11:25.144 --> 01:11:27.224
Those kids posted about that
on the internet too.

01:12:03.685 --> 01:12:05.769
This is about a pending case inquiry.

01:12:06.102 --> 01:12:09.852
A man named Ramesh
hanged himself in his apartment.

01:12:10.310 --> 01:12:12.661
Kavitha's number was one of
the last calls he made.

01:12:12.685 --> 01:12:15.538
Her number was saved on
his phone as "Kavitha, Koonanmukku".

01:12:15.723 --> 01:12:17.923
Why does this woman's name
keep popping up in this case?

01:12:17.977 --> 01:12:21.352
- Go to her house and look into it.
- Okay, sir.

01:12:21.560 --> 01:12:23.477
Keep an eye
on her house and the surroundings.

01:12:24.060 --> 01:12:26.240
- Try to meet her husband as well.
- Okay, sir.

01:12:26.435 --> 01:12:28.852
Sir, if the killer is actually based
near Koonanmukku

01:12:28.877 --> 01:12:31.037
then the geographical rule you mentioned
is spot on.

01:12:31.102 --> 01:12:34.370
Yes, sir. Justin was found
dead near Koonanmukku.

01:12:34.627 --> 01:12:37.547
And the spot where Boban was killed
is barely a kilometre away from there.

01:12:39.102 --> 01:12:41.269
We explored those possibilities
quite extensively.

01:12:42.255 --> 01:12:44.463
As a team, we've conducted
several studies.

01:12:44.487 --> 01:12:45.578
They were all correct.

01:12:45.602 --> 01:12:46.903
But the harsh reality is that

01:12:46.928 --> 01:12:49.124
we haven't made any real progress
on this particular case.

01:12:49.148 --> 01:12:50.435
We are right back at square one.

01:12:56.316 --> 01:12:58.578
Starting today, we are going to
take a different approach.

01:12:58.602 --> 01:13:00.602
- First, call off the night patrols.
- But sir...

01:13:00.644 --> 01:13:02.078
Wait, I'm coming to that.

01:13:02.227 --> 01:13:04.171
Instead,
we shift to covert night surveillance.

01:13:04.727 --> 01:13:06.927
We'll observe them directly,
and through hidden cameras.

01:13:06.977 --> 01:13:09.977
We will see everyone.
But no one will see us.

01:13:11.894 --> 01:13:13.935
That means... the killer will strike again...

01:13:15.102 --> 01:13:16.228
Exactly.

01:13:16.977 --> 01:13:18.452
Let the killer step out without fear

01:13:18.476 --> 01:13:20.168
and start hunting for his next victim.

01:13:20.435 --> 01:13:21.602
But this is a dangerous game.

01:13:21.769 --> 01:13:24.227
If we slip up even a little,
it's game over for all of us.

01:13:26.060 --> 01:13:27.233
It's a solid plan, sir.

01:13:27.310 --> 01:13:29.060
It's the fastest way to crack the case.

01:13:29.727 --> 01:13:31.355
We will execute it flawlessly, sir.

01:13:32.069 --> 01:13:33.892
Sojan sir, Basheer, are you guys on board?

01:13:33.977 --> 01:13:35.265
I'm in.

01:13:36.269 --> 01:13:37.375
Good.

01:13:37.602 --> 01:13:40.042
Ensure all the other investigations
continue at the same pace.

01:13:43.060 --> 01:13:45.477
Basheer, step into my office. Deepu...

01:13:50.685 --> 01:13:51.785
Hello.

01:13:51.810 --> 01:13:54.666
I rewatched your episode
on the Boban case.

01:13:54.810 --> 01:13:56.976
You recreated the murder to look like

01:13:57.000 --> 01:13:59.602
the killer attacked
because Boban provoked him.

01:13:59.727 --> 01:14:02.060
Why did you script it that way?

01:14:02.560 --> 01:14:05.019
I thought it would make
the show more interesting.

01:14:05.102 --> 01:14:08.352
Besides, the circumstantial
evidence pointed in that direction.

01:14:08.727 --> 01:14:12.227
But our investigation shows that Boban
was completely innocent.

01:14:12.477 --> 01:14:15.019
There's no way he provoked anyone.

01:14:16.102 --> 01:14:18.644
What if the killer was even more innocent?

01:14:19.810 --> 01:14:23.394
What if he got scared of Boban at
that moment and killed him on impulse?

01:14:23.894 --> 01:14:25.602
Moreover, Boban was drunk.

01:14:26.310 --> 01:14:28.894
Anyway, psycho killers
don't need reasons.

01:14:29.727 --> 01:14:31.160
That's true.

01:14:31.519 --> 01:14:34.502
And Christy,
when someone strikes out of fear,

01:14:34.526 --> 01:14:36.227
the first blow is always the hardest.

01:14:36.977 --> 01:14:38.523
To avoid getting hit back.

01:14:40.060 --> 01:14:44.477
So you think the killer is
a coward and he's scared.

01:14:45.060 --> 01:14:46.119
Right?

01:14:46.144 --> 01:14:47.352
That's a strong possibility.

01:14:47.658 --> 01:14:49.173
Maybe he's killing
one person after another

01:14:49.197 --> 01:14:50.602
just to overcome his own fear

01:14:50.852 --> 01:14:53.310
like a form of self-appreciation.

01:16:51.935 --> 01:16:53.335
What are you doing here?

01:16:53.894 --> 01:16:56.810
Oh, you seem to be hanging around
here all the time these days.

01:16:57.685 --> 01:16:58.871
Today is Sunday.

01:16:59.269 --> 01:17:01.569
According to your schedule,
it's the day to buy chicken.

01:17:01.935 --> 01:17:03.227
Adi will get the chicken.

01:17:03.727 --> 01:17:05.185
You go buy the other groceries.

01:17:06.477 --> 01:17:08.227
Some of his friends are coming over.

01:17:08.352 --> 01:17:10.192
They are planning to make Biryani.

01:17:11.293 --> 01:17:13.020
You go. I'll clean the floors.

01:17:14.685 --> 01:17:17.185
I'll clean the floors. You
go ahead. Put the broom down.

01:17:20.602 --> 01:17:22.786
Buy the groceries before
you start cleaning up.

01:17:22.810 --> 01:17:24.310
Does he not sleep at night or what?

01:17:35.477 --> 01:17:37.894
This is the one I told you about. Try it, sir.

01:17:38.144 --> 01:17:39.602
Mhm.

01:17:41.060 --> 01:17:42.226
Hey.

01:17:43.560 --> 01:17:45.202
He claims he was in the military.

01:17:45.227 --> 01:17:47.244
But apparently, he just
handled the laundry there.

01:17:47.269 --> 01:17:50.310
He's made a ton of money.
Shops like crazy every day.

01:17:51.560 --> 01:17:53.120
Who all lives at his house?

01:17:53.352 --> 01:17:55.102
His wife and her relatives.

01:17:55.435 --> 01:17:57.560
He doesn't get along
with his own relatives.

01:17:58.352 --> 01:18:01.352
Sir, are you planning to write
a story about Koonanmukku?

01:18:02.310 --> 01:18:04.150
Well, they say every
person has a unique story…

01:18:26.310 --> 01:18:27.894
"Convict gets parole after 10 years."

01:18:28.477 --> 01:18:30.870
"Marakkudi mass murder case."

01:18:30.894 --> 01:18:33.894
"The chilling memories of
the Marakkudi house."

01:18:41.685 --> 01:18:44.560
What's the matter, sir?
Adi went out to play.

01:18:44.727 --> 01:18:45.987
Come here.

01:18:52.002 --> 01:18:54.968
How are you connected to that
Ramesh guy who committed suicide?

01:18:55.185 --> 01:18:56.310
Why do you ask, madam?

01:18:57.144 --> 01:19:00.102
He bought some saplings from me.

01:19:00.477 --> 01:19:02.519
But you never mentioned
this business earlier.

01:19:03.144 --> 01:19:04.810
I run a small nursery here.

01:19:05.185 --> 01:19:07.644
People buy saplings from me sometimes.

01:19:08.519 --> 01:19:11.352
I also help people find rental houses.

01:19:11.810 --> 01:19:13.336
I just didn't bring it up that day.

01:19:13.435 --> 01:19:16.644
You are one of the last people who
called Ramesh before he died.

01:19:17.019 --> 01:19:18.259
We're here to investigate that.

01:19:19.189 --> 01:19:20.828
Please come in.
I'll get you something to drink.

01:19:20.852 --> 01:19:22.043
No, thank you.

01:19:27.060 --> 01:19:28.102
Where is your husband?

01:19:29.144 --> 01:19:30.397
He went to the shop, madam.

01:19:30.644 --> 01:19:32.578
That's the only help
you ever get from him, isn't it?

01:19:32.602 --> 01:19:33.644
I admire you.

01:19:34.019 --> 01:19:36.145
Anyone else would have
left a man like that long ago.

01:19:36.727 --> 01:19:37.769
He is my cousin, madam.

01:19:38.445 --> 01:19:39.700
When he was young,

01:19:39.724 --> 01:19:41.724
his father killed his mother
and committed suicide.

01:19:41.852 --> 01:19:43.438
He had to witness the whole thing.

01:19:43.894 --> 01:19:45.644
After that, my dad took him in.

01:19:46.269 --> 01:19:48.060
Since Vinayan was his late sister's son,

01:19:48.761 --> 01:19:50.881
my dad decided a long time ago
that I would marry him.

01:19:51.102 --> 01:19:53.828
Vinayan won't have anyone
else to support him if I leave too.

01:19:55.394 --> 01:19:59.477
Okay. I will handle Ramesh's case.

01:20:21.769 --> 01:20:23.578
He is a harmless guy, sir.

01:20:23.602 --> 01:20:25.269
He's terrified of everything.

01:20:25.383 --> 01:20:27.786
Do you remember me telling you
about a dog?

01:20:27.810 --> 01:20:31.019
Until it died, he was
too scared to even walk down this road.

01:20:34.102 --> 01:20:35.394
Where was this dog found dead?

01:20:35.944 --> 01:20:38.785
You see that pipe over there?
Right next to it.

01:21:39.685 --> 01:21:47.685
"Convict gets parole after 10 years."

01:22:03.339 --> 01:22:07.422
Sir, I'm only accepting this parole
because you worked so hard for it.

01:22:08.297 --> 01:22:09.837
To be completely honest,

01:22:09.862 --> 01:22:12.213
I'm a bit terrified
to go back into the real world.

01:22:12.797 --> 01:22:14.089
Why are you scared, Nawas?

01:22:14.756 --> 01:22:17.176
You'll feel better once you
go out and see your people.

01:22:17.631 --> 01:22:19.982
You had so many friends back home, right?

01:22:20.422 --> 01:22:23.202
Once they see you, they'll be
fine with you. Just go have a good time.

01:22:23.464 --> 01:22:24.682
Okay, then.

01:22:38.422 --> 01:22:39.668
Brother

01:22:39.839 --> 01:22:42.072
do you remember
the small dirt road near your house?

01:22:42.297 --> 01:22:45.339
It's a tarred road now.
A lot of new houses have come up.

01:22:47.047 --> 01:22:48.733
The whole place has changed completely.

01:22:48.955 --> 01:22:51.071
You might not even recognise it.

01:22:51.096 --> 01:22:52.472
The change is so drastic.

01:22:55.131 --> 01:22:58.464
I was just thinking that you haven't
changed a bit after all these years.

01:22:58.489 --> 01:22:59.650
Really?

01:22:59.757 --> 01:23:01.503
Look at you. You haven't changed either.

01:23:01.762 --> 01:23:03.815
Just pretend you were
working abroad, say in London,

01:23:03.839 --> 01:23:06.199
and now you're just
coming home for vacation. That's all.

01:23:31.297 --> 01:23:32.977
This whole area was overgrown with bushes.

01:23:33.089 --> 01:23:35.172
I cleared it up as much as I could.

01:23:35.506 --> 01:23:37.214
All the plants Zeenath planted were dead.

01:23:37.704 --> 01:23:40.371
So I planted some new flowers over there.

01:23:57.631 --> 01:23:59.951
All the old vessels in
your kitchen were completely rusted.

01:24:00.724 --> 01:24:04.016
I've arranged a few new ones
for you to use for now.

01:24:04.382 --> 01:24:07.770
But except for your PVC pipes
and a couple of taps,

01:24:07.795 --> 01:24:09.425
all your plumbing tools were ruined.

01:24:09.714 --> 01:24:11.849
I dumped them all in that corner.

01:24:11.873 --> 01:24:13.060
Come on in.

01:24:19.589 --> 01:24:21.549
Brother, shall we eat?

01:24:21.962 --> 01:24:22.981
Okay.

01:24:23.006 --> 01:24:26.670
My wife made some
really good beef curry and rice.

01:24:27.332 --> 01:24:29.464
And I brought some of Mom's tuna pickle.

01:24:33.855 --> 01:24:34.980
Brother

01:24:35.381 --> 01:24:37.672
you should go and see Zeenath tomorrow.

01:24:38.567 --> 01:24:40.127
If she is willing, bring her back here.

01:24:40.672 --> 01:24:41.832
You only have a few days.

01:24:41.881 --> 01:24:43.511
Make them memorable.

01:24:46.547 --> 01:24:50.381
What if Zeenath is still terrified of me?

01:24:51.338 --> 01:24:53.578
If she's scared, won't seeing her
just make things worse?

01:24:55.839 --> 01:24:57.815
Then why did you even come
home on parole, brother?

01:24:57.839 --> 01:24:59.179
Just to see me?

01:25:00.964 --> 01:25:04.422
Brother, a screw just came a bit loose
in your head back then.

01:25:05.256 --> 01:25:08.172
It's all fixed now. We all know that.

01:25:08.297 --> 01:25:09.339
Zeenath knows that too.

01:25:10.631 --> 01:25:12.464
That is all in the past.

01:25:13.797 --> 01:25:15.156
Go wash your hands.

01:25:24.672 --> 01:25:26.025
- Akbar…
- Yes.

01:25:26.214 --> 01:25:29.106
You said the news of my parole
was in the newspaper, right?

01:25:29.131 --> 01:25:31.162
Then Zeenath must know I'm back.

01:25:31.422 --> 01:25:32.709
Yes.

01:25:34.885 --> 01:25:36.514
I am not going anywhere.

01:25:37.131 --> 01:25:38.677
Let Zeenath come here if she wants to.

01:25:38.756 --> 01:25:40.124
Don't you think that's better?

01:25:43.172 --> 01:25:44.312
Brother

01:25:44.672 --> 01:25:46.200
when you were in prison,

01:25:46.224 --> 01:25:49.672
you had doctors and officers
to take care of you.

01:25:50.589 --> 01:25:52.381
Think about Zeenath.

01:25:55.047 --> 01:25:57.087
She was left all alone,
through no fault of her own.

01:26:00.756 --> 01:26:03.276
Don't think I am taking her side
just because she's my relative.

01:26:04.297 --> 01:26:05.785
You should go see her.

01:26:06.789 --> 01:26:08.190
Help her get over that fear.

01:26:09.993 --> 01:26:12.577
If Nizar and Uncle are your problem,
I will talk to them.

01:26:14.236 --> 01:26:16.736
Let them come visit you
when you go back to prison.

01:26:16.934 --> 01:26:18.502
I am not coming again.

01:26:19.368 --> 01:26:20.549
I mean it.

01:26:31.631 --> 01:26:34.846
My dad needs help just to go to the toilet.

01:26:34.871 --> 01:26:36.273
He won't let anybody else.

01:26:36.429 --> 01:26:37.843
Otherwise, I would have stayed here.

01:26:37.867 --> 01:26:39.142
It's alright.

01:26:39.339 --> 01:26:41.256
Just come over tomorrow after work.

01:26:41.598 --> 01:26:44.107
I just want to go out. I've been longing
to see the outside world.

01:26:44.131 --> 01:26:45.732
I'll take care of that. I should get going.

01:26:45.756 --> 01:26:46.817
Okay.

01:31:15.194 --> 01:31:16.402
Do you remember me?

01:31:16.427 --> 01:31:17.653
Swamy sir, right?

01:31:19.047 --> 01:31:21.756
I knew you would never forget me, Nawas.

01:31:22.297 --> 01:31:23.964
But sir, why are you here at this hour?

01:31:25.839 --> 01:31:27.214
I came to see you.

01:31:27.881 --> 01:31:29.214
It's been a long time.

01:31:30.047 --> 01:31:32.922
A cop can't just visit a convict
during the day when people are around.

01:31:35.422 --> 01:31:37.714
I heard you resigned
from the police department.

01:31:40.006 --> 01:31:41.486
There was one more case left pending.

01:31:42.297 --> 01:31:44.881
I came here to close that one too.

01:31:45.672 --> 01:31:47.631
Hmm. I heard about that case.

01:31:48.922 --> 01:31:51.547
If you are the investigating
officer, it will be closed soon.

01:31:55.339 --> 01:31:57.381
Please come in, sir. I'll
make some black tea.

01:31:58.339 --> 01:32:00.714
No, Nawas. Come for a drive with me.

01:32:02.089 --> 01:32:04.386
We can roam around a bit.

01:32:04.410 --> 01:32:07.547
We can talk,
and I can get some work done too.

01:32:27.547 --> 01:32:30.047
Circle Inspector Christy
tried to meet you in prison,

01:32:30.214 --> 01:32:32.256
but the superintendent didn't allow it.

01:32:32.506 --> 01:32:33.881
Why did he want to meet me?

01:32:37.047 --> 01:32:40.589
I think he wanted to study
your mental state at the time of the crime.

01:32:41.464 --> 01:32:44.714
The current case also
involves a psycho killer.

01:32:45.506 --> 01:32:47.131
What can I say about my mental state?

01:32:47.922 --> 01:32:50.339
I just lost my mind
for a moment. That's it.

01:32:51.547 --> 01:32:53.756
When I saw that little
girl on the balcony

01:32:54.422 --> 01:32:56.274
at first, I thought it was my daughter.

01:32:57.672 --> 01:32:59.131
Then I realised it wasn't.

01:33:00.172 --> 01:33:02.339
I felt like I was possessed.

01:33:03.714 --> 01:33:06.547
That's the only reason I am in
this situation today.

01:33:08.756 --> 01:33:11.547
You got proper treatment
and you are completely normal now.

01:33:11.672 --> 01:33:12.898
So what?

01:33:13.422 --> 01:33:14.797
Will normal people ever trust me?

01:33:16.256 --> 01:33:19.172
They will always be terrified
of a man who killed four people.

01:33:21.089 --> 01:33:24.217
Can the people who loved me

01:33:24.241 --> 01:33:27.672
and people closely with me
ever look at me the same way?

01:33:29.381 --> 01:33:31.101
Do you know why that is, Nawas?

01:33:31.589 --> 01:33:37.381
A regular criminal can stop committing
crimes if he simply decides to.

01:33:38.172 --> 01:33:40.381
But that's not the case for a psycho killer.

01:33:41.297 --> 01:33:44.547
Even he doesn't know when
he might lose his mind again.

01:33:46.339 --> 01:33:48.881
Do you think I'm going to lose
my mind again?

01:33:49.881 --> 01:33:53.922
I received the best treatment
possible for two and a half years.

01:33:55.214 --> 01:33:57.556
The doctors and the prison officials are

01:33:57.581 --> 01:33:59.935
very confident in my recovery.
That's why I am here now.

01:34:01.839 --> 01:34:04.256
I wasn't talking about you, Nawas.

01:34:05.881 --> 01:34:07.839
I'm talking from my own experience.

01:34:10.172 --> 01:34:13.381
Yours was the sixth psycho
case I investigated.

01:34:14.062 --> 01:34:15.270
While you were in prison,

01:34:15.294 --> 01:34:17.672
Ayyappan, the convict from
my very first case

01:34:18.339 --> 01:34:22.922
was released after treatment
because he was deemed a mental patient.

01:34:24.589 --> 01:34:27.089
The very first thing he did
was try to kill me.

01:34:28.172 --> 01:34:31.672
I quit my job and left town
out of pure fear of him.

01:34:32.839 --> 01:34:34.339
Let's drop this topic now.

01:34:34.714 --> 01:34:36.307
Let's talk about something else, sir.

01:34:37.922 --> 01:34:40.785
When I was granted parole,
the superintendent strictly told me

01:34:40.810 --> 01:34:43.810
not to listen to or discuss things like this.

01:34:48.872 --> 01:34:50.922
Actually, you should be doing
the exact opposite.

01:34:51.214 --> 01:34:52.500
You should see everything.

01:34:52.589 --> 01:34:53.967
You should listen to everything.

01:34:54.499 --> 01:34:56.152
You need the self-confidence
to know that

01:34:56.177 --> 01:34:58.397
you won't lose your mind
no matter what you face.

01:35:25.172 --> 01:35:26.845
That is exactly why

01:35:26.869 --> 01:35:30.381
I brought you here,
even though you might hate it.

01:35:45.672 --> 01:35:49.797
I wanted to visit this house
before returning to prison.

01:35:50.797 --> 01:35:53.381
I thought you'd be furious
with me for bringing you here.

01:35:53.714 --> 01:35:54.880
Why would I?

01:35:55.019 --> 01:35:58.199
Usually, nobody has the nerve
to revisit their own crime scene.

01:35:59.839 --> 01:36:01.517
I don't have the nerve either.

01:36:02.121 --> 01:36:04.129
But I felt so, somehow.

01:36:05.922 --> 01:36:07.256
Then go inside and come back.

01:36:07.547 --> 01:36:09.214
We'll find out the truth right now.

01:36:10.589 --> 01:36:11.662
Find out what truth?

01:36:12.714 --> 01:36:14.172
When you step inside that house

01:36:14.422 --> 01:36:16.422
if you feel a sense of euphoria

01:36:16.881 --> 01:36:19.631
then that psycho is
still alive inside you.

01:36:20.631 --> 01:36:23.714
But if you feel
overwhelming guilt and regret

01:36:24.589 --> 01:36:26.297
then you are completely cured.

01:39:39.006 --> 01:39:40.086
Nawas

01:39:40.256 --> 01:39:42.119
there is absolutely
nothing wrong with you.

01:39:42.547 --> 01:39:44.233
You are perfectly normal.

01:39:46.187 --> 01:39:47.661
Your mind is clean.

01:39:48.131 --> 01:39:49.216
But…

01:40:43.527 --> 01:40:45.944
- Good morning, sir.
- Good morning. Come, let's sit inside.

01:40:47.652 --> 01:40:49.698
Have you come across
someone named Vinayan

01:40:49.777 --> 01:40:52.444
at any point during your investigation?

01:40:55.985 --> 01:40:57.318
Vinayan?

01:40:58.860 --> 01:41:00.597
Yes, a man whose name came up

01:41:00.621 --> 01:41:03.574
at various stages of our investigation.
But we just ignored him.

01:41:04.444 --> 01:41:07.360
There is a kid named Adityan
on your suspect list, right?

01:41:08.360 --> 01:41:09.735
It's his dad. Vinayan.

01:41:10.902 --> 01:41:12.378
We did look into them,

01:41:12.402 --> 01:41:15.569
but we couldn't find anything
suspicious about the family…

01:41:28.694 --> 01:41:31.735
I asked around about him at Koonanmukku.

01:41:38.819 --> 01:41:41.194
Just as we thought, he is short,

01:41:42.110 --> 01:41:44.860
and he has an innocent face
that wouldn't scare anyone.

01:41:45.610 --> 01:41:47.402
He is terrified of everyone.

01:41:50.235 --> 01:41:53.735
There was a dog that used to bark
and scare him

01:41:54.444 --> 01:41:57.194
it was found dead, with its
head smashed against a rock.

01:41:57.902 --> 01:42:02.194
A few days later, Justin
was murdered in the exact same way.

01:42:03.444 --> 01:42:05.627
I know about the feud
between Justin and Adityan.

01:42:05.652 --> 01:42:07.317
But there's one thing I don't understand.

01:42:07.860 --> 01:42:09.427
Just because of an issue with his son,

01:42:09.452 --> 01:42:11.707
would someone this terrified
kill a guy like Justin?

01:42:13.110 --> 01:42:16.194
What if Justin was just another dog
that was barking and scaring Vinayan?

01:42:16.694 --> 01:42:18.402
He killed the dog out of pure fear.

01:42:21.319 --> 01:42:22.319
But what about Boban?

01:42:24.402 --> 01:42:26.048
That is for you to figure out.

01:42:29.194 --> 01:42:30.474
Anyway, I'll keep an eye on him.

01:42:31.985 --> 01:42:34.610
Anyway, I'll keep an eye on him.
Your intuition is never wrong.

01:42:45.277 --> 01:42:48.235
Find out if he has a habit of
wandering around alone at night.

01:42:49.944 --> 01:42:51.694
I already looked into that.

01:42:54.860 --> 01:42:56.966
Then how come your cameras
haven't caught him yet?

01:42:58.235 --> 01:43:00.181
We will review the CCTV
footage again, sir.

01:43:04.860 --> 01:43:08.319
He'll try to kill anyone who frightens him.

01:43:08.610 --> 01:43:12.902
So arrest him immediately and
see if his fingerprints match.

01:43:15.277 --> 01:43:16.777
Will do, sir.

01:43:42.069 --> 01:43:44.628
We can't just put an ad in the paper
saying we've stopped night patrols.

01:43:44.652 --> 01:43:47.420
Sir, I think the killer is still
spooked by the police and won't come out.

01:43:47.444 --> 01:43:48.566
Sojan, hold on.

01:44:01.985 --> 01:44:03.005
Hello.

01:44:03.194 --> 01:44:04.425
Hello, Kavitha.

01:44:04.527 --> 01:44:05.691
This is Jenny.

01:44:05.777 --> 01:44:07.336
The police officer who
visited the other day.

01:44:07.360 --> 01:44:08.860
Yes, madam.

01:44:09.027 --> 01:44:10.877
I need a few saplings.

01:44:10.902 --> 01:44:13.860
Can I swing by after work?
Will you be there?

01:44:14.569 --> 01:44:16.610
You don't need to come all the way here
for that.

01:44:16.819 --> 01:44:19.085
I will bring them to the
police station this afternoon.

01:44:19.365 --> 01:44:21.127
Why can't I come home?

01:44:21.152 --> 01:44:23.277
Are you upset that I
questioned you the other day?

01:44:23.652 --> 01:44:25.735
There's no need for that.
I was just doing my job.

01:44:26.360 --> 01:44:27.485
It's not that, madam.

01:44:28.569 --> 01:44:31.860
Ever since that incident, Vinayan
has been terrified of the police.

01:44:32.110 --> 01:44:34.343
Especially if you show
up in a police jeep...

01:44:35.485 --> 01:44:38.027
Well then, I'm definitely coming over.

01:44:38.360 --> 01:44:39.902
Let's help him get over his fear.

01:44:40.485 --> 01:44:41.585
Is he there?

01:44:41.610 --> 01:44:44.058
Yes, madam. He's here.
He's still sleeping.

01:44:45.027 --> 01:44:46.485
Does he not sleep at night?

01:44:47.735 --> 01:44:50.194
Just text me his phone number.

01:44:50.630 --> 01:44:52.002
I'll summon him to the station.

01:44:52.027 --> 01:44:53.610
You can send the saplings with him.

01:44:54.152 --> 01:44:55.498
We can't go easy on him.

01:44:56.194 --> 01:44:57.838
He doesn't own a mobile phone, madam.

01:44:57.944 --> 01:44:59.084
He has no one to call.

01:44:59.152 --> 01:45:01.650
Please just tell me what you need.
I'll bring them to you.

01:45:02.402 --> 01:45:05.402
It's fine. I'll call you
and drop by another day.

01:45:06.030 --> 01:45:07.370
Okay, madam.

01:45:07.853 --> 01:45:10.944
When you visited Kavitha's place, her husband wasn't there, right?
-Yes.

01:45:11.074 --> 01:45:12.503
Were you able to get any info on him?

01:45:12.527 --> 01:45:14.681
Like his background,
childhood… anything like that?

01:45:15.235 --> 01:45:18.195
His father murdered his mother and
hanged himself when Vinayan was a kid.

01:45:18.444 --> 01:45:19.794
He was raised by his uncle.

01:45:19.819 --> 01:45:21.350
By uncle, I mean Kavitha's dad.

01:45:21.610 --> 01:45:26.485
Kavitha was forced into marrying him
because he's her cousin and an orphan.

01:45:29.069 --> 01:45:30.860
I think Swamy's intuition is spot on.

01:45:31.316 --> 01:45:33.895
We lost him,
even though he was right in front of us.

01:45:35.235 --> 01:45:36.661
We haven't lost him yet.

01:45:38.110 --> 01:45:42.277
Jenny, you and Basheer stake out
his house and stay there.

01:45:43.027 --> 01:45:45.187
- Sojan and his team will get there by night.
- Yes, sir.

01:45:45.319 --> 01:45:49.169
Like Swamy said, you need to see
if he sneaks out of the house at night.

01:45:49.194 --> 01:45:52.569
If he steps out, nab him immediately.

01:45:52.667 --> 01:45:53.673
Okay, sir.

01:45:53.777 --> 01:45:55.215
Any updates from Basheer?

01:46:08.485 --> 01:46:10.878
It was the woman next door who
reported it after seeing the door open.

01:46:10.902 --> 01:46:12.402
- When did it happen?
- Last night.

01:46:12.556 --> 01:46:14.771
- Have you identified the body?
- It's Nawas, who was out on parole.

01:46:14.795 --> 01:46:17.045
- His friend Akbar identified the body.
- Is the forensic team here?

01:46:17.069 --> 01:46:19.419
They are at another crime scene.
They'll be late.

01:46:19.444 --> 01:46:20.770
There's no power here.

01:46:20.819 --> 01:46:22.420
So we've asked them
to get here before dusk.

01:46:22.444 --> 01:46:23.557
Won't Swamy sir come?

01:46:23.610 --> 01:46:24.903
It would be good if he did.

01:46:25.027 --> 01:46:26.916
He won't show up because of the media.

01:46:27.027 --> 01:46:30.227
Even otherwise, these overhyped guys
are useless in a real crisis.

01:46:30.610 --> 01:46:31.922
- Sir...
- Yeah?

01:46:32.860 --> 01:46:34.711
It'll be blood all over.
Should I go check it out?

01:46:34.735 --> 01:46:37.469
- No. Just check the perimeter.
- Yes, sir.

01:46:37.552 --> 01:46:40.294
And see if there's any evidence
of someone visiting here regularly.

01:46:40.319 --> 01:46:41.516
Will do, sir.

01:48:09.510 --> 01:48:10.723
The pattern matches.

01:48:10.777 --> 01:48:11.990
A frontal attack.

01:48:12.069 --> 01:48:13.652
No signs of a struggle from the victim.

01:48:14.027 --> 01:48:15.420
It's exactly the same.

01:48:15.569 --> 01:48:18.819
So you think it's the same killer?

01:48:19.264 --> 01:48:21.625
I'm just wondering how the
old psycho and the new psycho

01:48:21.650 --> 01:48:23.110
ended up in this house together.

01:48:23.569 --> 01:48:25.929
Call the forensic team and tell them
to rush the procedures.

01:48:25.985 --> 01:48:27.875
- Yes, sir.
- Call them right now. - Yes, sir.

01:48:29.485 --> 01:48:31.736
We need to cross-check
the fingerprints from all

01:48:31.760 --> 01:48:34.194
three crime scenes to
draw a definitive conclusion.

01:48:34.860 --> 01:48:38.819
But for Justin and Boban,
Vinayan is still our prime suspect.

01:48:39.235 --> 01:48:40.575
We can bring him in, sir.

01:48:42.569 --> 01:48:44.330
By the time
the fingerprint reports come in

01:48:44.354 --> 01:48:45.709
I want Vinayan in custody.

01:48:45.735 --> 01:48:46.788
Yes, sir.

01:48:46.830 --> 01:48:47.961
Sojan sir…

01:49:38.110 --> 01:49:41.860
The Marakkudi mass murder.

01:49:53.152 --> 01:49:57.027
Based on what you said, the killer
we're dealing with is "act-focused."

01:49:57.569 --> 01:50:00.319
But Nawas' murder was clearly premeditated.

01:50:00.985 --> 01:50:04.078
Someone who has been waiting for
Nawas for ten years did this.

01:50:05.902 --> 01:50:09.860
Maybe the victims' relatives
finally took their revenge.

01:50:10.319 --> 01:50:11.545
No, Maria.

01:50:11.944 --> 01:50:14.735
I'm seeing the makings of
another serial killer in this case.

01:50:15.444 --> 01:50:16.817
Let me explain.

01:50:17.694 --> 01:50:19.712
Swamy told me about
a very specific feeling you get

01:50:19.736 --> 01:50:22.112
when you observe a crime scene
with an open mind.

01:50:22.694 --> 01:50:24.660
I experienced that for
the very first time today.

01:50:24.777 --> 01:50:27.152
While I was examining Nawas'
body and the area around it,

01:50:27.402 --> 01:50:28.569
I had an intuition.

01:50:41.319 --> 01:50:44.299
Someone familiar with the methods used in
the Justin and Boban murders

01:50:44.444 --> 01:50:47.464
someone brilliant enough to
manipulate a police investigation,

01:50:47.562 --> 01:50:49.202
and someone who personally knew Nawas.

01:50:49.277 --> 01:50:50.929
I can only think of one such person.

01:50:51.860 --> 01:50:53.255
Swamy.

01:50:56.027 --> 01:50:57.902
But why would Swamy kill Nawas?

01:50:58.944 --> 01:51:01.360
Nawas is the sixth psycho Swamy caught.

01:51:01.819 --> 01:51:02.902
The first one was Ayyappan.

01:51:03.194 --> 01:51:04.794
Do you know the history of Ayyappan?

01:51:04.819 --> 01:51:07.002
- The guy who murdered his own wife and child?
- Yes.

01:51:07.027 --> 01:51:12.319
I know he was released after his treatment
because he was classified as mentally ill.

01:51:13.069 --> 01:51:15.360
Ayyappan tried to murder Swamy
the moment he was released.

01:51:16.194 --> 01:51:18.412
I read in this file that
Ayyappan's body was later

01:51:18.437 --> 01:51:20.757
found on a railway track
under suspicious circumstances.

01:51:21.652 --> 01:51:23.860
I have studied all six
of Swamy's cases in detail.

01:51:24.485 --> 01:51:26.165
It's not just Ayyappan and Nawas.

01:51:26.235 --> 01:51:28.944
Not a single one of
those six men is alive today.

01:51:33.444 --> 01:51:36.157
Just because these six people died
under suspicious circumstances

01:51:36.235 --> 01:51:38.595
how can we jump to the conclusion
that Swamy killed them?

01:51:38.902 --> 01:51:41.961
Most of these killers end up like that
once they are released from prison anyway.

01:51:41.985 --> 01:51:43.028
Yes.

01:51:43.115 --> 01:51:45.295
No matter how they die,
the investigation is just a formality.

01:51:45.319 --> 01:51:47.569
There's no one
to even speak on their behalf.

01:51:48.152 --> 01:51:50.569
Swamy took advantage of
that and killed those five,

01:51:51.277 --> 01:51:52.319
and now Nawas.

01:51:54.194 --> 01:51:56.319
Why is Swamy waiting for them
just to kill them?

01:51:57.027 --> 01:51:58.235
What's his motive?

01:51:58.777 --> 01:52:00.803
Sir, his problem is fear.

01:52:01.152 --> 01:52:03.842
He is terrified that the culprits
he arrested when he was

01:52:03.866 --> 01:52:06.444
in the service will kill him
once they are released.

01:52:06.610 --> 01:52:08.050
That's his issue.

01:52:08.995 --> 01:52:10.650
When the first convict came to kill him,

01:52:10.674 --> 01:52:12.942
Swamy panicked,
resigned, and ran away.

01:52:13.152 --> 01:52:15.753
He won't even stay in one
place for too long because of his paranoia.

01:52:15.777 --> 01:52:18.735
Even when you tried to track him down
for our case, you couldn't find him.

01:52:20.235 --> 01:52:23.035
That's why he showed up here at the
exact time of Nawas' parole, right?

01:52:23.985 --> 01:52:25.621
When he was caught
during our routine check,

01:52:25.645 --> 01:52:27.638
he told Sojan he came to visit a friend.

01:52:27.735 --> 01:52:29.965
He played everyone
perfectly - the police

01:52:29.989 --> 01:52:32.194
department, the situation,
and above all, me.

01:52:44.944 --> 01:52:46.177
By the way,

01:52:46.610 --> 01:52:50.527
we didn't form a special team
just to investigate Swamy.

01:52:51.652 --> 01:52:54.402
If we don't close the
Justin and Boban case,

01:52:55.027 --> 01:52:56.777
will anyone believe a word we say?

01:52:58.819 --> 01:53:01.069
What happened to the suspect you mentioned?

01:53:01.819 --> 01:53:03.359
We are bringing him in tonight, sir.

01:53:04.152 --> 01:53:05.912
Sojan and Basheer are
staking out his house.

01:53:06.152 --> 01:53:09.985
Along with him, if you give us
permission to arrest Swamy as well…

01:53:12.277 --> 01:53:16.360
In Swamy's case, it's all just your
assumptions and guesses.

01:53:18.652 --> 01:53:19.985
But if you are that confident

01:53:21.194 --> 01:53:22.334
go ahead.

01:53:23.569 --> 01:53:24.869
Thank you, sir.

01:54:13.444 --> 01:54:14.597
Hello.

01:54:15.610 --> 01:54:18.319
Hello, sir. We aren't waiting
for the forensic report on Nawas.

01:54:18.860 --> 01:54:22.551
We are going to arrest Vinayan
based on the clues you gave us.

01:54:22.604 --> 01:54:23.691
That's good.

01:54:23.735 --> 01:54:25.992
Along with the news of the third murder,

01:54:26.069 --> 01:54:28.170
let the photo of the culprit
hit the newspapers as well.

01:54:28.194 --> 01:54:30.485
For solving such a complicated case,

01:54:30.652 --> 01:54:32.832
Christy and his team will earn
a solid reputation.

01:54:33.194 --> 01:54:34.397
Sir,

01:54:34.629 --> 01:54:37.429
this is the first time I'm feeling
that thrill during an investigation.

01:54:37.610 --> 01:54:40.027
You taught me a lot.

01:54:41.110 --> 01:54:44.860
Wishing you the best in solving many more
unresolved cases. Congratulations.

01:54:47.110 --> 01:54:48.735
Sir, it's too early for congratulations.

01:54:49.944 --> 01:54:53.010
If the fingerprints from the crime
scenes don't match Vinayan's,

01:54:53.235 --> 01:54:54.677
I'll be back to square one.

01:54:54.777 --> 01:54:58.527
The fingerprints from all three crime
scenes will match Vinayan's.

01:54:58.819 --> 01:55:00.225
I am absolutely sure.

01:55:00.444 --> 01:55:01.735
Hmm. Okay, sir.

01:58:38.194 --> 01:58:40.795
Sir, let me explain. If they know
each other, it's extremely dangerous.

01:58:40.819 --> 01:58:41.985
Their common trigger is fear.

01:58:42.152 --> 01:58:43.860
So we can't predict who will kill who.

01:58:43.980 --> 01:58:47.120
- We need to find them immediately.
- The police will take care of catching them.

01:58:47.735 --> 01:58:50.294
We have passed the information
to all stations and check-posts.

01:58:50.319 --> 01:58:52.694
Before dawn, both of them
will be in our custody.

01:59:26.944 --> 01:59:29.527
Will the police hurt me?

01:59:30.944 --> 01:59:32.694
No, don't be afraid.

01:59:36.610 --> 01:59:40.277
I'll have to spend a
long time in prison, right?

01:59:46.694 --> 01:59:50.027
Will the court hang me? Huh?

01:59:50.194 --> 01:59:51.480
No. Never.

01:59:58.610 --> 02:00:00.610
Will they give me three meals a day
in prison?

02:00:03.735 --> 02:00:05.361
Food?

02:00:25.985 --> 02:00:26.985
In that case

02:00:27.777 --> 02:00:32.694
I can live peacefully in prison
without fearing anyone.

02:00:35.527 --> 02:00:36.694
Without fearing anyone.

02:00:38.402 --> 02:00:39.575
But

